WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:02:49.654 --> 00:02:50.584
600 to dispatch,

00:02:50.584 --> 00:02:53.134
what you got running on this, go on?

00:02:53.134 --> 00:02:53.967
To 600,

00:02:53.967 --> 00:02:56.774
we haven't been able to
dispatch anybody yet.

00:02:57.607 --> 00:03:00.684
Six oh one to dispatch.

00:03:00.684 --> 00:03:04.601
Six oh one establish
command at 6th and Harvey.

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:15.020
On April 19th, 1995,

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:17.270
as many people were
starting their workday,

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:20.300
a beautiful spring morning
in the heartland became chaos

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:23.270
when at 9:02 A.M., explosions tore through

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:25.050
the Alfred p. Murrah federal building

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.080
in downtown Oklahoma city.

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:28.910
An explosion at
nine o'clock this morning

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:31.170
that did that damage you're
looking at right there,

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:34.830
blowing off the entire
north face of that building.

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:37.700
- The federal building located
200 north west 5th street

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:39.780
was almost completely destroyed.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:42.890
- A terrible tragedy has
occurred here in Oklahoma city.

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:44.390
- The bombing in Oklahoma city

00:03:45.356 --> 00:03:48.043
was an attack on innocent children,

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:50.750
and defenseless citizens.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:52.590
168 people were killed

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:55.240
in the blast and over 800 wounded.

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:57.910
The hospitals were
overrun with casualties.

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:00.060
A rescue worker was
killed from falling debris

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:02.350
within the first few hours.

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:05.360
But what would sear the bombing
in the hearts of Americans

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:06.750
was the 19 children

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:09.040
inside the daycare center in the building

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.990
who had lost their lives.

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:13.860
The most beautiful
memorial left by anyone

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:16.730
is not in the rubble of this building,

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:19.270
but in the hearts and
the lives that knew them

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:20.830
and loved them.

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:23.300
We come today to remember their lives,

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.510
and we come today to offer thanks.

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:27.677
Thanks for the hundreds
and hundreds of people

00:04:27.677 --> 00:04:31.160
who were involved in the
rescue and recovery efforts.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:32.940
Six years before 9/11,

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:34.790
it was the first mass casualty

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:36.793
terrorist attack on American soil.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:40.050
The prologue to a new
chapter in American history

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:43.010
had been written in
blood, fear, and shock.

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:44.870
Terrorism had struck home.

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:47.543
From now on, nothing
would be the same again.

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:53.810
- We know that more than McVeigh
and Nichols were involved.

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:56.220
- There were questions of other bombs

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:58.400
being found at the scene of the crime,

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.070
witnesses to the bombing.

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:02.010
- The FBI, like any government agency,

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:05.120
is more concerned with power, prestige,

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:08.840
maintaining its position,
rather than truth and justice.

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:11.898
- Based on the damage
pattern to the building,

00:05:11.898 --> 00:05:13.750
what the government said is impossible.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:16.890
- That life we had back
before the bombing,

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:18.510
that life is over.

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:21.000
- For the first time in my
fight with the government,

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.637
they stepped forward and said,

00:05:22.637 --> 00:05:25.475
"it would pose a grave risk
to the national security

00:05:25.475 --> 00:05:26.470
of the United States of America

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:28.780
if we release these CIA documents."

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:31.023
- If you know the truth,
the truth will set you free.

00:05:31.023 --> 00:05:35.740
- You've got to band together
or it's over for all of us.

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:37.960
The man on top will get you.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:39.620
- If we don't expose the facts

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:42.000
that Oklahoma city stinks to high heaven,

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.317
the same people that carried it out

00:05:43.317 --> 00:05:45.960
are going to do it over,
and over, and over again.

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:47.850
And they're going to use
these frightening events

00:05:47.850 --> 00:05:50.040
to drive a stake through the United States

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:51.323
and kill our republic.

00:05:56.930 --> 00:05:58.090
Almost immediately

00:05:58.090 --> 00:05:59.860
the Oklahoma city police department

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:01.470
announced a "be on the lookout" alert

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:03.580
for two middle eastern looking suspects

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:05.173
wearing blue jogging suits.

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:07.770
Shortly before the bombing,

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:10.380
they were seen by a witness
running from the murrah building

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:12.400
and getting into a brown pickup truck,

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:15.280
then driving away from
the scene of the crime.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:17.267
It was soon determined that a truck bomb

00:06:17.267 --> 00:06:20.150
had exploded directly
outside the building.

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:22.880
Approximately 200 feet
from the bomb crater,

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:25.019
a vin number, stamped on a twisted axle,

00:06:25.019 --> 00:06:28.123
identified the vehicle
as a Ryder rental truck.

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:31.540
- Two suspects are in custody
this evening in the bombing

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:34.090
of Oklahoma city's
murrah federal building.

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:35.420
Shortly after the bombing,

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:37.500
a 26 year old U.S. army veteran,

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.360
Timothy McVeigh, was pulled over by

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:41.500
an Oklahoma highway patrol officer,

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:44.200
60 miles north of Oklahoma city.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:45.920
He was stopped for speeding in his car

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.120
without a license plate.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.560
McVeigh would admit to
carrying a concealed handgun,

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:53.440
and was taken into
custody without incident.

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:55.730
It was the first time Timothy McVeigh

00:06:55.730 --> 00:06:57.353
had been arrested in his life.

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:01.780
The original alert for
two middle eastern males

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:04.380
had been rescinded within
hours of the bombing.

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:07.130
And the identification
number on the Ryder axle

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:10.090
was traced to a rental agency in Kansas.

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:12.150
The renter had given a false name,

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:14.550
but had listed his address as a farmhouse

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:17.300
in Michigan belonging to James Nichols.

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:20.370
James's brother Terry Nichols
was a friend of Tim McVeigh

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:22.470
from their time in the U.S. army.

00:07:22.470 --> 00:07:24.270
Upon hearing the news that he was wanted

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:25.910
for questioning in the bombing,

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:27.560
Terry Nichols turned himself

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:29.910
in to the harrington,
Kansas police department.

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:33.420
Within 24 hours after the attack,

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:36.080
the FBI had received a
tip from a former coworker

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:38.550
of Tim McVeigh in buffalo, New York.

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:40.900
The tipster informed the FBI that McVeigh

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:43.982
had often espoused militant
antigovernment views

00:07:43.982 --> 00:07:46.310
and that McVeigh was very angry

00:07:46.310 --> 00:07:48.060
over the siege of the branch davidians

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:50.580
by federal agents in waco, Texas,

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:52.910
which had ended in a catastrophic fire

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:55.610
two years to the day before
the Oklahoma city bombing.

00:07:57.300 --> 00:08:02.300
- That Friday they showed
the FBI bringing Tim McVeigh

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:06.240
out of the jail in Perry, Oklahoma.

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:09.350
And that's when I got angry.

00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:12.020
When I saw that it was an American

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:14.053
and it wasn't middle easterners.

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:17.720
I had a hard time accepting the fact

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:20.780
that Americans would do that.

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:23.650
Americans are supposed
to love their children.

00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:27.980
They're not supposed to
murder their children.

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:31.140
- Shaken, disillusioned, angered

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:36.093
that that could happen in this country.

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:40.100
Upon learning that
McVeigh was already in jail,

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:42.730
the FBI transferred him to federal custody

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:45.570
and an indictment was
issued against Tim McVeigh,

00:08:45.570 --> 00:08:47.730
Terry Nichols, and others unknown

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:50.570
for the bombing of the
murrah federal building.

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:52.330
Another army buddy of McVeigh's,

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:54.600
Michael fortier of Kingman, Arizona,

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:56.560
was later arrested and charged

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:59.110
with having advanced
knowledge of the bombing plot.

00:09:03.473 --> 00:09:07.460
- The last thing I
remember was being thrown

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:09.770
to the center of that room and looking up

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:14.770
and looking into the sky,
and there was no roof

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:17.470
and everything was just
suspended up in the air,

00:09:17.470 --> 00:09:18.560
in the sky.

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:21.350
- When I came to, I stood
up facing the south,

00:09:21.350 --> 00:09:22.950
but all the light was behind me.

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:26.930
I turned, looked back to the north

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:29.836
and the whole front of
the building's gone.

00:09:29.836 --> 00:09:33.960
I'm about, oh, four to five
feet from where it dropped off.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:38.300
- On the morning of April 19th,
1995, my dog, gunny and I,

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:41.070
arrived at the scene
of the murrah building.

00:09:41.070 --> 00:09:43.363
There was a great deal
of chaos at the scene.

00:09:44.357 --> 00:09:45.470
A lot of people bleeding,

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:48.090
screaming, running away from the building.

00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:49.580
- I lost my two grandchildren.

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:53.030
They were in the daycare
center at the murrah building.

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:57.140
Their names were Aaron
and Elijah Coverdale.

00:09:57.140 --> 00:09:58.710
Aaron was five years old.

00:09:58.710 --> 00:10:00.520
Elijah was two.

00:10:00.520 --> 00:10:04.220
I was living at the regency
when the bombing happened.

00:10:04.220 --> 00:10:06.430
That morning I was at work.

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:08.560
I had custody of Aaron and Elijah

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:10.360
so they lived with me.

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:12.680
And I had dropped them
off at the daycare center

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:14.570
that Wednesday morning.

00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:17.700
I'd get up in the middle of
the night and get in the shower

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:20.470
and turn the water on so people
wouldn't hear me screaming.

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:25.031
And I'd just scream at god
and ask him, "what was wrong?

00:10:25.031 --> 00:10:28.020
Why were we being punished so?"

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:32.223
- I knew the Coverdale
boys, Elijah and Aaron.

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:35.000
These two boys, they were characters.

00:10:36.514 --> 00:10:38.880
Me being single and
living in this apartment,

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:41.970
I was kind of a party guy
at that time, 27 years old.

00:10:41.970 --> 00:10:45.437
At one point in time, I
had promised these two boys

00:10:45.437 --> 00:10:48.120
that I was gonna give them some toys.

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:50.730
And problem with that,
living in the regency,

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:52.640
you know, 18th floor, you
leave something in your car,

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:54.870
you don't wanna go back down and get it

00:10:54.870 --> 00:10:57.510
because it's just a hassle
unless it's ice cream.

00:10:57.510 --> 00:11:00.737
And so, I left these toys in
the car for the longest time.

00:11:00.737 --> 00:11:05.737
And I never did get them
those toys until, you know,

00:11:06.803 --> 00:11:10.410
after they passed away,
when I gave them to jannie.

00:11:10.410 --> 00:11:12.530
- Well, I got watching the
stuff down on the street.

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:14.625
I kinda got mesmerized by what

00:11:14.625 --> 00:11:15.900
was going on down on the street.

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:18.610
While I was standing up
there, there was a little girl

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:20.760
that was taking a photography class at uco

00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:26.730
that took a picture of the building

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:29.530
and I was in that picture.

00:11:29.530 --> 00:11:33.560
- You could not see
anything in front of you.

00:11:33.560 --> 00:11:37.963
It was so, the smoke was
so thick and so Black.

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:43.390
And the only thing I can tell
you is it smelled like sulfur.

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:47.200
If you were in a chemistry
lab, it smelled like sulfur.

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:49.660
And she said, "you can't go that way."

00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:50.580
And I said, "why?"

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:52.900
She said, "there is nothing out there.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:54.191
It's gone."

00:12:02.730 --> 00:12:04.880
The reasons for
the bombing, the perpetrators,

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:06.840
the rumors, and the suspects change

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:09.210
depending on whose viewpoint you take.

00:12:09.210 --> 00:12:10.800
Like all controversial events,

00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:12.570
some of those closest to the event,

00:12:12.570 --> 00:12:14.550
and farthest away, are bound together

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:16.700
by their questioning
of the official story.

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:19.110
The first questions were directed

00:12:19.110 --> 00:12:21.610
at the bureau of alcohol,
tobacco, and firearms

00:12:21.610 --> 00:12:24.340
which had launched the raid
on the branch davidians.

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:26.310
The Oklahoma city office for the atf

00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:28.230
was located in the murrah building,

00:12:28.230 --> 00:12:30.740
and was the supposed target of the attack.

00:12:30.740 --> 00:12:33.743
Yet, no agents were killed
or seriously wounded.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:37.373
Was the atf office empty that morning?

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:42.250
- I'm asking if I can
speak with an atf officer

00:12:42.250 --> 00:12:44.600
that worked in the building
so I could find out

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:48.350
if they knew anything about my wife

00:12:49.220 --> 00:12:54.220
and he told me that they were
in debriefing and I asked him,

00:12:54.410 --> 00:12:56.617
you know, "I need to talk to one of 'em.

00:12:56.617 --> 00:12:58.820
I need to find out something."

00:12:58.820 --> 00:13:01.510
And he said that none of them
had been in the building,

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:02.590
so they weren't hurt.

00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:04.610
They had been tipped by their pagers

00:13:04.610 --> 00:13:06.750
that morning not to come into work.

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:09.960
The atf told
several different stories

00:13:09.960 --> 00:13:12.620
to explain their agents' curious absences.

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:15.220
The most fantastic story
was that two agents

00:13:15.220 --> 00:13:18.513
were indeed inside the building
and were heroes that day.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:21.610
Atf agent Luke franey claimed

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:22.820
that he was knocked unconscious

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:26.220
by the blast and after an
aborted helicopter rescue,

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:29.590
crawled onto an outside
ledge to escape his office.

00:13:29.590 --> 00:13:32.040
Franey reported that he then
used his martial arts skills

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:34.863
to break through several
walls and injured his hand.

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:38.380
Another agent, Alex mccauley,

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:39.830
claimed that he was in an elevator

00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:41.450
at the time of the bombing.

00:13:41.450 --> 00:13:43.580
After free falling for five floors,

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:46.923
mccauley supposedly broke out
and rescued several people.

00:13:49.070 --> 00:13:52.460
- My crews were the crews
working on the murrah building

00:13:52.460 --> 00:13:53.480
the day of the bombing.

00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:56.730
Immediately after the bombing,
they called me on the radios

00:13:56.730 --> 00:14:00.603
and at that point they were
going in to assist with,

00:14:00.603 --> 00:14:02.700
because the fire department
hadn't even got there yet.

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:03.750
They were going to check to make sure

00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:05.930
all the elevators were clear.

00:14:05.930 --> 00:14:07.840
They weren't aware,
because they were coming

00:14:07.840 --> 00:14:09.330
from the south side,

00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:12.700
that the building on
the north side was gone.

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:16.436
So they went in to check the
elevators and that's when

00:14:16.436 --> 00:14:19.470
they found out how bad the
damage was inside the building.

00:14:19.470 --> 00:14:21.050
None of the elevators went to free fall

00:14:21.050 --> 00:14:23.630
because the governor
overspeeds were not tripped.

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:26.030
The safety mechanisms on
the bottom of the elevators

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:27.330
were not tripped,

00:14:27.330 --> 00:14:29.730
none of the elevators had
a free fall condition.

00:14:30.911 --> 00:14:32.863
I think it was mccauley indicated

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:36.160
that they were trapped in an elevator,

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:38.720
so at the grand jury investigation,

00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:40.380
once I got the fema report that showed

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:41.550
which elevator they were in,

00:14:41.550 --> 00:14:44.090
I said that there's no possible way

00:14:44.090 --> 00:14:45.240
they could've been in that elevator

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:48.460
because my men checked it
and it was still locked

00:14:48.460 --> 00:14:50.963
from the top and the doors were,

00:14:52.420 --> 00:14:54.880
the wall had caved in against
the doors between floors,

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:55.810
so they couldn't have gotten out

00:14:55.810 --> 00:14:57.593
of the elevator without assistance.

00:14:58.490 --> 00:14:59.910
Jane Graham
worked in the building

00:14:59.910 --> 00:15:01.120
for over a decade,

00:15:01.120 --> 00:15:04.100
was vice president of the
federal employees union,

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:07.490
and has testified before
congress on labor issues.

00:15:07.490 --> 00:15:09.160
She knew everyone in the building,

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:11.810
and bore witness to suspicious
behavior that morning.

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:14.810
- On the morning of the bombing,

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:18.630
when my husband dropped me
off and I got out of the car,

00:15:18.630 --> 00:15:20.540
as I was walking toward the entrance,

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:22.917
there were two men standing

00:15:22.917 --> 00:15:26.560
directly in front of the double doors,

00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:29.900
and there was a little sitting area there,

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:32.010
planter and so forth there in front.

00:15:32.010 --> 00:15:34.360
They were standing right
there on the sidewalk.

00:15:34.360 --> 00:15:39.360
They had on atf jackets
which said, "atf" on them.

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:42.770
They were talking to a third gentleman

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:46.690
who was dressed in business clothes.

00:15:46.690 --> 00:15:48.000
And I saw them.

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:50.820
Their backs were to me and I thought,

00:15:50.820 --> 00:15:53.620
they don't normally, you know,

00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:56.600
all of the people we
see go up there to atf,

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:58.450
they're never identifiable.

00:15:58.450 --> 00:16:00.640
You know, they always
are dressed, you know,

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:03.460
a lot of 'em look like drug
people and other things.

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:05.060
You know, but they're
certainly not dressed

00:16:05.060 --> 00:16:07.093
for you to be able to tell who they are.

00:16:08.212 --> 00:16:09.760
A paramedic who responded

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:11.760
to the bombing, Tiffany Bible,

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:14.350
confirms that the atf
were not in their office,

00:16:14.350 --> 00:16:15.650
and, in fact, may have been aware

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:17.250
of some type of threat that day.

00:16:18.670 --> 00:16:19.830
In this affidavit,

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:21.940
she states that immediately
after the bombing,

00:16:21.940 --> 00:16:24.160
she asked an atf agent on the scene

00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:25.980
if any of them were in the building.

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:29.080
He responded, "no, we
weren't in there today."

00:16:29.080 --> 00:16:32.277
And that "the murrah building
was bombed because of waco."

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:35.170
She further states

00:16:35.170 --> 00:16:37.260
that within the first 20
minutes of the bombing,

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:39.660
she saw at least 8 atf agents

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:42.600
outside the building in
clean, Black jumpsuits.

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:44.640
To this day the atf has been unwilling

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:47.040
to address their prior
knowledge of the bombing.

00:16:49.660 --> 00:16:53.290
Beyond the vague rumors of the
significance of April 19th,

00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:57.360
some federal agencies were
aware of an actual threat.

00:16:57.360 --> 00:16:59.540
- One of the most frustrating
things about prior knowledge

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:02.560
is that the media, some in the media,

00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:04.990
and others would accuse us of saying

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:07.000
that the government blew the building up.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:09.210
Which we never said.

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:10.840
And I do not believe.

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:13.560
The U.S. marshals,
responsible for security

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:15.460
of federal personnel and facilities,

00:17:15.460 --> 00:17:18.130
warned that, quote, "islamic terrorists

00:17:18.130 --> 00:17:20.150
may be planning suicide attacks

00:17:20.150 --> 00:17:23.880
against federal courthouses
and government installations

00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:26.460
designed to attract
worldwide press attention

00:17:26.460 --> 00:17:28.970
through the murder of innocent victims."

00:17:28.970 --> 00:17:31.620
The atf had placed informant Carol howe

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:33.320
into a white separatist community

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:35.850
in eastern Oklahoma called elhoim city

00:17:35.850 --> 00:17:39.320
another atf agent admitted
under oath that one suspect,

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:41.967
Andy strassmeir, was
reported to make, quote,

00:17:41.967 --> 00:17:44.720
"threats to blow up federal
buildings", unquote,

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:46.870
before the Oklahoma city bombing.

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:49.010
Furthermore, Carol howe actually drove

00:17:49.010 --> 00:17:50.610
strassmeir and other suspects

00:17:50.610 --> 00:17:53.800
to Oklahoma city to scout bombing targets.

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:56.880
Was this the source of the
atf suspicious behavior

00:17:56.880 --> 00:17:58.303
the morning of April 19th?

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:02.020
U.S. representative Ernest
istook, of Oklahoma,

00:18:02.020 --> 00:18:04.990
also displayed advanced
knowledge of the bombing.

00:18:04.990 --> 00:18:06.730
- To my left, from the east,

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:10.470
I saw senator istook
kinda work his way west.

00:18:10.470 --> 00:18:14.020
Well, he came up to me and we
started talking small talk.

00:18:14.020 --> 00:18:15.770
You know, terrible thing and all this,

00:18:15.770 --> 00:18:18.640
and really didn't know what much to say.

00:18:18.640 --> 00:18:20.647
And he said, all of sudden
he made the comment,

00:18:20.647 --> 00:18:22.850
"yeah, we knew this was gonna happen."

00:18:22.850 --> 00:18:24.350
- I noticed the lady back behind me

00:18:24.350 --> 00:18:26.600
by a backhoe over there taking pictures.

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:31.600
She identified herself as an
attorney, Lanny, Lana Tyree,

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:33.860
and she was with Ernest istook.

00:18:33.860 --> 00:18:36.660
And she made a comment to
me that istook told her

00:18:36.660 --> 00:18:39.360
that they were aware of a
bomb threat since April 9th.

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:42.658
We didn't really think much
about it until this grand jury

00:18:42.658 --> 00:18:45.030
started probing into it
and people were claiming

00:18:45.030 --> 00:18:47.060
that there wasn't any prior knowledge.

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:49.370
But, you know, I start thinking
about it and got with Dave,

00:18:49.370 --> 00:18:50.960
and we put two and two together,

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:54.010
and we said, "hey, somebody
knew about a prior bomb threat.

00:18:54.010 --> 00:18:55.570
You know, this ought to be known."

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:58.370
- Everyone who knows me
knows I would not sit idle

00:18:58.370 --> 00:19:01.030
if I knew about a conspiracy of silence.

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:04.600
I would never rest until such
a conspiracy was exposed.

00:19:04.600 --> 00:19:07.380
But I know of no such conspiracy.

00:19:07.380 --> 00:19:09.670
Istook has denied
this evidence under oath,

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:11.160
but he has never answered

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:13.710
the Oklahoma county
sheriff's deputy's challenge

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:16.870
to subject his opposing
versions of prior knowledge

00:19:16.870 --> 00:19:18.193
to polygraph testing.

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:27.940
Many witnesses have officially stated

00:19:27.940 --> 00:19:30.790
that the Oklahoma county bomb
squad was conducting a search

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:33.010
at the federal courthouse
across the street

00:19:33.010 --> 00:19:35.660
from the murrah building
two hours before the attack.

00:19:36.680 --> 00:19:38.740
- Trish nix, I ran into her.

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:41.660
She was another employee there at hud.

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:44.710
And she had asked me if I had seen

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:47.000
the bomb squad that morning.

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:50.830
And I had said, "no, I wasn't aware

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:52.420
that they had been in the building."

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:53.630
And she said, "yes."

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:57.801
She had seen their unit
parked in the parking lot

00:19:57.801 --> 00:20:00.773
of the church across the street.

00:20:01.870 --> 00:20:03.370
County appraiser j.D. Reed

00:20:03.370 --> 00:20:04.870
saw the bomb disposal unit

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:07.113
parked outside the
courthouse that morning.

00:20:08.210 --> 00:20:10.080
Despite multiple eyewitnesses,

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:12.280
the sheriff's department
denies this claim.

00:20:12.280 --> 00:20:13.920
- If that building was under threat,

00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:15.970
and they were getting bomb threats,

00:20:15.970 --> 00:20:18.590
and this was a daily
thing, or a weekly thing,

00:20:18.590 --> 00:20:21.980
or if they've gotten many
threats, or only one,

00:20:21.980 --> 00:20:24.530
the parents of the
children in that daycare

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:26.550
deserved to have been notified.

00:20:26.550 --> 00:20:29.810
People do not keep children in daycares

00:20:29.810 --> 00:20:32.391
where there are bomb threats made.

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:36.840
Under the
pressure of mounting evidence,

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:40.030
abc's "20/20" reported on many
of these puzzling questions

00:20:40.030 --> 00:20:42.230
a year and a half after the bombing.

00:20:42.230 --> 00:20:43.510
- At issue, increasingly,

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:45.680
for some of the victims
and their families,

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:49.120
what did authorities know or
suspect before the explosion,

00:20:49.120 --> 00:20:51.140
that federal workers and the children

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:52.440
arriving at the murrah building

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:55.150
did not know or were not told?

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:56.960
There was this fairly large truck

00:20:56.960 --> 00:20:58.840
with a trailer behind it

00:20:58.840 --> 00:21:00.920
and it had a shield on
the side of the door,

00:21:00.920 --> 00:21:03.700
and it said, "bomb disposal"
or "bomb squad" below it.

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:04.880
Authorities now claim,

00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:07.140
in federal investigative reports,

00:21:07.140 --> 00:21:10.160
that the huge ominous
truck with its trailer,

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:14.060
was being used by a deputy
to run routine errands.

00:21:14.060 --> 00:21:17.580
Other documents obtained by
"20/20" show that someone called

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:19.380
the executive secretariat's office

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:22.207
at the justice department
in Washington and said,

00:21:22.207 --> 00:21:24.750
"the murrah building had been bombed."

00:21:24.750 --> 00:21:27.760
But this was 24 minutes before the blast.

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:30.140
No action was apparently taken.

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:31.720
According
to the show's producer

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:34.360
the justice department
actively intervened to prevent

00:21:34.360 --> 00:21:35.970
an in-depth follow up to this segment

00:21:35.970 --> 00:21:37.193
from airing nationally.

00:21:39.731 --> 00:21:44.731
- "20/20" did a 15 or 20 minute
segment on prior knowledge.

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:48.000
It was put together by a
guy named Roger Charles.

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:52.470
That was so explosive that
he was putting together

00:21:52.470 --> 00:21:55.590
an entire hour or whatever for "20/20",

00:21:55.590 --> 00:21:57.430
which he would tell you.

00:21:57.430 --> 00:21:59.420
But the feds came in and stopped "20/20."

00:21:59.420 --> 00:22:02.490
Wouldn't let them broadcast
the larger segment

00:22:02.490 --> 00:22:04.890
that he put together
concerning prior knowledge.

00:22:06.452 --> 00:22:07.370
- The news channel has learned

00:22:07.370 --> 00:22:08.690
of another strange development.

00:22:08.690 --> 00:22:11.040
Apparently before the bombing,

00:22:11.040 --> 00:22:12.960
governor frank keating's brother Mark

00:22:12.960 --> 00:22:14.120
had been working on a novel

00:22:14.120 --> 00:22:16.170
about a terrorist
bombing in Oklahoma city.

00:22:16.170 --> 00:22:18.851
Stranger still, one of the
characters in the novel

00:22:18.851 --> 00:22:20.940
was named Thomas McVeigh.

00:22:20.940 --> 00:22:22.440
Despite the official denials,

00:22:22.440 --> 00:22:23.490
the evidence confirms

00:22:23.490 --> 00:22:26.530
that at least some amount
of prior knowledge existed.

00:22:26.530 --> 00:22:28.287
More ominously, there are suggestions

00:22:28.287 --> 00:22:30.450
that certain government agencies

00:22:30.450 --> 00:22:33.720
were fully expecting a
bombing to occur that day.

00:22:33.720 --> 00:22:36.410
- The horse patrol, interestingly,

00:22:36.410 --> 00:22:39.710
was a very small unit, and was assisted

00:22:39.710 --> 00:22:43.803
by the county reserve mounted patrol unit.

00:22:45.540 --> 00:22:48.820
For whatever reason, on
the morning of the bombing,

00:22:48.820 --> 00:22:51.800
they had been assigned and had already met

00:22:51.800 --> 00:22:56.230
at the Oklahoma city
equine and canine facility.

00:22:56.230 --> 00:22:59.470
And had prepared their horses, their tack,

00:22:59.470 --> 00:23:03.780
and uniforms to go
downtown for crowd control.

00:23:03.780 --> 00:23:06.878
Rarely, very rarely would
they go down and patrol

00:23:06.878 --> 00:23:11.220
or work the downtown area for
crowd control, for anything.

00:23:11.220 --> 00:23:13.230
The importance
of exposing prior knowledge

00:23:13.230 --> 00:23:14.970
cannot be understated.

00:23:14.970 --> 00:23:17.720
Those individuals who
understood the danger beforehand

00:23:17.720 --> 00:23:20.030
and did nothing are just as guilty

00:23:20.030 --> 00:23:22.153
as those who lit the fuse on the bomb.

00:23:29.400 --> 00:23:31.430
As the FBI and department of justice

00:23:31.430 --> 00:23:33.210
narrowed its focus on Tim McVeigh

00:23:33.210 --> 00:23:35.410
as the lone bomber on April 19th,

00:23:35.410 --> 00:23:38.300
people seeking truth and justice
for the dead were dismayed

00:23:38.300 --> 00:23:40.030
that so many reports of accomplices

00:23:40.030 --> 00:23:43.020
were being discarded by
the federal authorities.

00:23:43.020 --> 00:23:46.480
The first sketches of the
suspects released by the FBI

00:23:46.480 --> 00:23:49.210
clearly indicated that
two people were involved

00:23:49.210 --> 00:23:52.150
in parking the Ryder truck in
front of the murrah building.

00:23:52.150 --> 00:23:54.980
And the original bola, or
"be on the lookout alert"

00:23:54.980 --> 00:23:56.960
had mentioned three suspects.

00:23:56.960 --> 00:23:59.560
When the hunt for John
Doe #2 was called off

00:23:59.560 --> 00:24:03.110
and he was dismissed as a ghost,
people who knew for a fact

00:24:03.110 --> 00:24:05.000
that they had seen
McVeigh with other people,

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:06.203
began to speak out.

00:24:07.200 --> 00:24:08.983
Did McVeigh act alone?

00:24:12.680 --> 00:24:15.570
- During that time
broadcasts were being made

00:24:15.570 --> 00:24:19.070
that there was suspects had been observed

00:24:19.070 --> 00:24:21.580
leaving the scene in a brown pickup.

00:24:21.580 --> 00:24:23.840
- At this time people were
trying to get together

00:24:23.840 --> 00:24:28.580
on who was going to do what,
medical personnel and such.

00:24:28.580 --> 00:24:30.782
There was a police car sitting to my left

00:24:30.782 --> 00:24:35.160
facing west on 5th street

00:24:35.160 --> 00:24:37.770
and as we were all standing
there, conversing, and you know,

00:24:37.770 --> 00:24:39.680
people were doing what they were doing,

00:24:39.680 --> 00:24:42.550
it came out over the
radio on this police car,

00:24:42.550 --> 00:24:45.560
that they were looking for a brown truck.

00:24:45.560 --> 00:24:48.110
An apb for a brown truck.

00:24:48.110 --> 00:24:50.000
It was quick.

00:24:50.000 --> 00:24:51.200
But it was heard.

00:24:51.200 --> 00:24:53.507
- I haven't stopped asking questions,

00:24:53.507 --> 00:24:57.033
because I know that we
haven't been told the truth.

00:24:58.380 --> 00:25:00.220
I've talked to too many people

00:25:00.220 --> 00:25:03.240
that saw Timothy McVeigh that morning,

00:25:03.240 --> 00:25:06.150
saw Timothy McVeigh in Kansas,

00:25:06.150 --> 00:25:09.270
and saw Timothy McVeigh in Oklahoma city.

00:25:09.270 --> 00:25:12.480
Not one person saw him by himself.

00:25:12.480 --> 00:25:14.050
- Timothy McVeigh
stepped out of the truck.

00:25:14.050 --> 00:25:15.183
I walked him over to,

00:25:17.050 --> 00:25:19.800
let's say 10, 11 feet away
from the truck itself.

00:25:19.800 --> 00:25:22.700
I pointed a direction
downtown, which is to my right.

00:25:22.700 --> 00:25:26.200
He seemed to acknowledge
where I was talking about.

00:25:26.200 --> 00:25:28.070
At that time, the gentleman
walked back to the truck.

00:25:28.070 --> 00:25:29.190
I talked to him, I also noticed

00:25:29.190 --> 00:25:32.330
there was a passenger in
the truck at that time.

00:25:32.330 --> 00:25:33.990
- And mostly it was a John Doe two thing,

00:25:33.990 --> 00:25:35.650
because you remember,

00:25:35.650 --> 00:25:38.540
it was the greatest
manhunt there's ever been.

00:25:38.540 --> 00:25:41.923
And then all of a sudden,
"hey, he doesn't even exist."

00:25:41.923 --> 00:25:45.150
If he doesn't exist, what was
the deal about the manhunt?

00:25:45.150 --> 00:25:46.130
I mean things like that.

00:25:46.130 --> 00:25:47.830
That was continually coming out.

00:25:47.830 --> 00:25:52.380
- I know for a fact Timothy McVeigh

00:25:52.380 --> 00:25:56.360
was with another individual
on the morning of April 19th

00:25:56.360 --> 00:25:57.713
right before the bombing.

00:25:58.660 --> 00:26:03.130
- Because the evidence is
overwhelming and compelling

00:26:03.130 --> 00:26:04.770
that there were other perpetrators,

00:26:04.770 --> 00:26:06.944
and they were not pursued.

00:26:06.944 --> 00:26:09.868
In the very early days after the bombing

00:26:09.868 --> 00:26:12.290
the decision was made not to pursue

00:26:12.290 --> 00:26:13.803
any more of those individuals.

00:26:17.440 --> 00:26:19.410
In the days
before the bombing Tim McVeigh

00:26:19.410 --> 00:26:22.240
was seen making preparations
with other suspects.

00:26:22.240 --> 00:26:24.550
Not Terry Nichols, or Michael fortier,

00:26:24.550 --> 00:26:25.710
but others unknown,

00:26:25.710 --> 00:26:29.110
whom the authorities seemed
uninterested in finding.

00:26:29.110 --> 00:26:31.350
- The man that I saw
on the phone that day,

00:26:31.350 --> 00:26:33.853
that was actually on
the phone was McVeigh.

00:26:35.160 --> 00:26:37.010
I'm 100% sure of that.

00:26:37.010 --> 00:26:40.400
He had a partner with him
that had shoulder-length hair,

00:26:40.400 --> 00:26:42.950
that was leaned up against
the wall facing him.

00:26:42.950 --> 00:26:45.790
Then at one point he turned
to the guy to his right,

00:26:45.790 --> 00:26:48.530
who was leaning against the
wall, shoulder-length hair,

00:26:48.530 --> 00:26:51.067
and said, "he told us
to stay here."

00:26:53.170 --> 00:26:56.790
I did go up to the FBI at 50 penn place

00:26:56.790 --> 00:26:58.900
and told them my story.

00:26:58.900 --> 00:26:59.733
If I remember right,

00:26:59.733 --> 00:27:03.075
I think they actually
sketched out the second person

00:27:03.075 --> 00:27:06.260
that I was describing,

00:27:06.260 --> 00:27:10.678
which was shoulder-length
hair, tan, stocky build,

00:27:10.678 --> 00:27:15.500
a light plaid type jacket shirt kinda mix,

00:27:15.500 --> 00:27:16.853
kinda goofy looking guy.

00:27:17.900 --> 00:27:20.530
A convenience
store clerk reported to the FBI

00:27:20.530 --> 00:27:23.110
that McVeigh had purchased
fuel for a Ryder truck

00:27:23.110 --> 00:27:25.590
at her store two days before the bombing,

00:27:25.590 --> 00:27:27.600
even pointing out on the register tape

00:27:27.600 --> 00:27:29.420
when the purchase was made.

00:27:29.420 --> 00:27:32.200
Accompanying McVeigh was another suspect.

00:27:32.200 --> 00:27:34.990
This example is only one
of many eyewitness accounts

00:27:34.990 --> 00:27:37.640
that diverge from the official narrative.

00:27:37.640 --> 00:27:39.100
And although the government states

00:27:39.100 --> 00:27:41.680
that McVeigh never scouted
inside the murrah building,

00:27:41.680 --> 00:27:44.560
a secret service investigator
reported that she had seen him

00:27:44.560 --> 00:27:47.303
in the building, also
with a second suspect.

00:27:51.640 --> 00:27:54.320
The official narrative
dictates that Tim McVeigh alone

00:27:54.320 --> 00:27:56.700
rented the Ryder truck
in junction city, Kansas

00:27:56.700 --> 00:28:00.250
on April 17, two days before the bombing.

00:28:00.250 --> 00:28:02.590
He and Terry Nichols
supposedly constructed the bomb

00:28:02.590 --> 00:28:04.200
on April 18th.

00:28:04.200 --> 00:28:06.370
But the bulk of eyewitness accounts assert

00:28:06.370 --> 00:28:08.410
that the Ryder truck was at geary lake

00:28:08.410 --> 00:28:09.860
for several days before that.

00:28:10.700 --> 00:28:15.570
- I retired April 11, 1995

00:28:15.570 --> 00:28:19.867
and after finishing up that morning,

00:28:19.867 --> 00:28:24.230
I decided to stop by here
and fish at geary state lake,

00:28:24.230 --> 00:28:27.850
which is right in this general area here

00:28:27.850 --> 00:28:32.850
that I was fishing from,
the pier, or jetty.

00:28:32.920 --> 00:28:36.540
And I stayed here most
of the afternoon fishing,

00:28:36.540 --> 00:28:37.933
of course with no luck.

00:28:38.900 --> 00:28:41.730
And later on that afternoon

00:28:41.730 --> 00:28:46.730
I had decided to maybe go
back over this way over here

00:28:47.260 --> 00:28:50.460
to the other point back there
and see if I'd have any luck.

00:28:50.460 --> 00:28:55.260
When I noticed a Ryder truck over there.

00:28:55.260 --> 00:28:57.610
I was sitting at home one day
and my wife came in from work

00:28:57.610 --> 00:28:59.250
and she said that she had been stopped

00:28:59.250 --> 00:29:00.130
at a Road block up here

00:29:00.130 --> 00:29:04.770
at geary lake in reference
to the Oklahoma city bombing.

00:29:04.770 --> 00:29:06.400
And the making of the bomb here

00:29:06.400 --> 00:29:09.487
at geary state lake with a Ryder truck.

00:29:09.487 --> 00:29:11.580
And I said, "well, you
know, I had told you

00:29:11.580 --> 00:29:16.580
about the Ryder truck I had
seen there before this."

00:29:16.780 --> 00:29:18.840
And that's how I became aware of it.

00:29:18.840 --> 00:29:23.080
And then the next thing I
knew, she told the atf and FBI,

00:29:23.080 --> 00:29:25.343
the people at the
roadblock, what I had seen.

00:29:26.757 --> 00:29:29.764
And before I knew it, my
house was swarming with

00:29:29.764 --> 00:29:32.193
agents.

00:29:36.200 --> 00:29:38.040
McVeigh stayed
at the dreamland motel

00:29:38.040 --> 00:29:40.760
just outside the gates
of fort Riley, Kansas

00:29:40.760 --> 00:29:43.200
while he rented the
truck and built the bomb.

00:29:43.200 --> 00:29:46.550
Once again, eyewitnesses
state that he was not alone

00:29:46.550 --> 00:29:48.290
and the Ryder truck was there for days

00:29:48.290 --> 00:29:50.373
before the FBI insists it was.

00:29:52.680 --> 00:29:53.870
The maid at the dreamland

00:29:53.870 --> 00:29:56.370
saw McVeigh's friend with the Ryder truck,

00:29:56.370 --> 00:29:59.957
and when shown a sketch of
John Doe #2, told the FBI,

00:29:59.957 --> 00:30:02.170
"my god, who did the sketch?

00:30:02.170 --> 00:30:03.497
It looks just like him."

00:30:04.510 --> 00:30:05.910
All these reports indicate

00:30:05.910 --> 00:30:08.710
that more than one Ryder truck
was involved in the bombing,

00:30:08.710 --> 00:30:11.363
and more people than the
government is letting on.

00:30:14.100 --> 00:30:17.610
- Justice for these
killers will be certain,

00:30:17.610 --> 00:30:19.563
swift, and severe.

00:30:20.720 --> 00:30:23.653
We will find them, we will convict them,

00:30:24.820 --> 00:30:27.580
and we will seek the
death penalty for them.

00:30:27.580 --> 00:30:28.980
It was promised to the people

00:30:28.980 --> 00:30:31.640
of Oklahoma city and
to the rest of america

00:30:31.640 --> 00:30:34.360
that every single person
responsible for the bombing

00:30:34.360 --> 00:30:37.180
would be caught, tried,
and held accountable

00:30:37.180 --> 00:30:39.340
for the harm they had inflicted.

00:30:39.340 --> 00:30:40.870
It was expected that this promise

00:30:40.870 --> 00:30:42.510
would be fulfilled.

00:30:42.510 --> 00:30:44.900
Nevertheless, as eyewitness testimony

00:30:44.900 --> 00:30:46.520
and other promising leads were being

00:30:46.520 --> 00:30:49.780
carelessly discarded,
replaced only with the lies

00:30:49.780 --> 00:30:52.163
and inconsistencies of federal officials,

00:30:54.330 --> 00:30:58.350
a deep but private suspicion
grew in the minds of observers

00:30:58.350 --> 00:31:00.010
that perhaps a government cover-up

00:31:00.010 --> 00:31:01.570
was underway.

00:31:01.570 --> 00:31:04.450
Was this mere incompetence
or was there something else

00:31:04.450 --> 00:31:05.990
at work here?

00:31:05.990 --> 00:31:08.750
- I was a police officer in
the Tulsa police department

00:31:08.750 --> 00:31:11.810
for 27 years, and in 1995,

00:31:12.739 --> 00:31:15.330
when the Oklahoma city bombing occurred,

00:31:15.330 --> 00:31:17.700
I was requested by the local FBI office

00:31:17.700 --> 00:31:19.250
through our chief of police to assist

00:31:19.250 --> 00:31:22.490
any way I could and look into the bombing

00:31:22.490 --> 00:31:25.190
and using my contacts as an
investigative journalist,

00:31:25.190 --> 00:31:28.330
which is what I did on the
side, to try to find out

00:31:28.330 --> 00:31:30.480
anything we could find
out about the bombing:

00:31:30.480 --> 00:31:33.720
McVeigh, Nichols, and just kind of follow

00:31:33.720 --> 00:31:35.500
the investigation anyplace it went.

00:31:35.500 --> 00:31:36.950
Just follow the leads.

00:31:36.950 --> 00:31:38.230
I was still working the case with

00:31:38.230 --> 00:31:40.350
jayna Davis and David Hoffman,

00:31:40.350 --> 00:31:42.300
two Oklahoma city police officers.

00:31:42.300 --> 00:31:43.980
And one of 'em, it was
one of the first ones

00:31:43.980 --> 00:31:45.990
in the building, and he saw some things

00:31:45.990 --> 00:31:47.710
in the building, he saw the biggest damage

00:31:47.710 --> 00:31:48.910
to the building was the pit,

00:31:48.910 --> 00:31:50.100
which was in the back of the building

00:31:50.100 --> 00:31:51.870
and went down, like, two or three floors.

00:31:51.870 --> 00:31:53.543
He saw all of that.

00:31:53.543 --> 00:31:56.420
That never came out in the news.

00:31:56.420 --> 00:31:58.940
It wasn't part of the investigation.

00:31:58.940 --> 00:32:00.240
It didn't count.

00:32:00.240 --> 00:32:02.590
In other words, if it didn't fit the mold

00:32:02.590 --> 00:32:05.165
that the department of
justice under Janet Reno set

00:32:05.165 --> 00:32:08.280
for the FBI, then it
wasn't put in the case.

00:32:08.280 --> 00:32:09.580
Period.

00:32:09.580 --> 00:32:11.300
The FBI
bragged about its handling

00:32:11.300 --> 00:32:14.080
of the deadliest terror
attack in American history,

00:32:14.080 --> 00:32:16.500
but gigantic holes in the
case were being ignored

00:32:16.500 --> 00:32:17.523
by the media.

00:32:18.480 --> 00:32:20.900
McVeigh was first suspected
because he rented the truck

00:32:20.900 --> 00:32:22.750
under the name Robert kling.

00:32:22.750 --> 00:32:24.590
One of the first pieces of evidence used

00:32:24.590 --> 00:32:27.264
to link McVeigh to the
bombing was problematic.

00:32:27.264 --> 00:32:29.310
- I went to junction city.

00:32:29.310 --> 00:32:31.300
I went out to Elliott's body shop

00:32:31.300 --> 00:32:33.205
and I spoke to Mr. Elliott.

00:32:33.205 --> 00:32:37.263
I told him who I was, and I said,

00:32:39.087 --> 00:32:41.830
"I would like for you to tell me

00:32:41.830 --> 00:32:44.560
what happened the day Tim came to rent

00:32:44.560 --> 00:32:46.430
the Ryder truck."

00:32:46.430 --> 00:32:49.907
And he said, "you mean, the
day Tim and his friend came?"

00:32:51.060 --> 00:32:54.260
And I said, "Tim wasn't by himself?"

00:32:54.260 --> 00:32:55.487
He said, "no, ma'am."

00:32:56.760 --> 00:32:59.000
- The FBI had been designated
by President Clinton

00:32:59.000 --> 00:33:02.013
as the lead federal agency
in this investigation.

00:33:05.360 --> 00:33:07.530
Incredibly enough, there remains

00:33:07.530 --> 00:33:10.563
an extra unidentified leg
that was found in the rubble.

00:33:11.590 --> 00:33:13.780
Oklahoma state medical
examiner Fred Jordan

00:33:13.780 --> 00:33:16.040
testified in court, "we had eight people

00:33:16.040 --> 00:33:18.310
with traumatically amputated left legs.

00:33:18.310 --> 00:33:20.379
However, we have nine left legs.

00:33:20.379 --> 00:33:22.137
We have one leg too many."

00:33:24.040 --> 00:33:26.270
Stephen Jones, McVeigh's defense attorney,

00:33:26.270 --> 00:33:28.195
detailed in his book, "others unknown,"

00:33:28.195 --> 00:33:30.770
the significance of this extra leg.

00:33:30.770 --> 00:33:32.940
Former chief pathologist
for northern Ireland,

00:33:32.940 --> 00:33:36.060
t.k. Marshall, performed
over 2,500 autopsies

00:33:36.060 --> 00:33:38.987
on bombing victims, and told Jones that,

00:33:38.987 --> 00:33:40.620
"in all the years in Ireland,

00:33:40.620 --> 00:33:42.490
we identified every innocent person

00:33:42.490 --> 00:33:43.610
that was killed.

00:33:43.610 --> 00:33:45.360
There was never an unknown victim."

00:33:47.900 --> 00:33:50.670
The FBI collected 1,034 fingerprints

00:33:50.670 --> 00:33:54.900
during their investigation, but
an agent admitted under oath

00:33:54.900 --> 00:33:56.630
that these prints were not run through

00:33:56.630 --> 00:33:58.830
the national fingerprint database.

00:33:58.830 --> 00:34:00.544
Niki deutchman was the jury foreperson

00:34:00.544 --> 00:34:03.220
for the federal trial of Terry Nichols.

00:34:03.220 --> 00:34:06.340
- I think that the government, perhaps,

00:34:06.340 --> 00:34:08.210
really dropped the ball.

00:34:08.210 --> 00:34:11.770
I think that there were a
large number of sightings

00:34:11.770 --> 00:34:13.373
right around before,

00:34:14.440 --> 00:34:17.510
the week before and the days and months

00:34:17.510 --> 00:34:19.460
after the bombing.

00:34:19.460 --> 00:34:22.193
And sketches of people
that were recognizable.

00:34:23.245 --> 00:34:27.170
In this trial, there even was a photograph

00:34:27.170 --> 00:34:30.350
of someone who may have been involved

00:34:30.350 --> 00:34:33.163
with mixing the bomb, with
putting the bomb together.

00:34:34.430 --> 00:34:36.140
And that person, it was a photograph

00:34:36.140 --> 00:34:37.400
from the newspaper, obviously,

00:34:37.400 --> 00:34:38.880
that person's identity is known.

00:34:38.880 --> 00:34:41.450
I think there are other people out there

00:34:41.450 --> 00:34:44.490
and decisions were
probably made very early on

00:34:44.490 --> 00:34:46.380
that Tim McVeigh and Terry Nichols

00:34:46.380 --> 00:34:48.120
were who they were looking for

00:34:48.120 --> 00:34:51.950
and the same sort of
resources were not used

00:34:51.950 --> 00:34:54.250
to try to find out who
else might be involved.

00:34:58.600 --> 00:35:01.250
- Well, in those first couple of days,

00:35:01.250 --> 00:35:04.330
especially that first day of
the Oklahoma city bombing,

00:35:04.330 --> 00:35:07.190
there was immediate
information that came out

00:35:07.190 --> 00:35:09.810
about what caused the bombing,

00:35:09.810 --> 00:35:11.720
witnesses on the scene of the crime,

00:35:11.720 --> 00:35:14.070
things such as that, and it changed

00:35:14.070 --> 00:35:17.120
very significantly and drastically

00:35:17.120 --> 00:35:20.380
as the day went by and the
next several days went by.

00:35:20.380 --> 00:35:22.770
That caused a lot of
questions in people's minds

00:35:22.770 --> 00:35:25.320
about what really happened here.

00:35:25.320 --> 00:35:28.010
- The reason I doubt, started doubting

00:35:28.010 --> 00:35:30.060
the official story that was comin' out,

00:35:30.060 --> 00:35:32.190
you have to understand that the state,

00:35:32.190 --> 00:35:36.120
the local media were doing a good job

00:35:36.120 --> 00:35:37.003
the first day.

00:35:38.270 --> 00:35:41.040
Local law enforcement,
maybe, also, I believe,

00:35:41.040 --> 00:35:42.520
was doing a good job.

00:35:42.520 --> 00:35:45.560
But once the feds came in,
things started changing.

00:35:45.560 --> 00:35:48.740
The police and emergency
crews are talking about

00:35:48.740 --> 00:35:51.480
moving us back because of the danger of,

00:35:51.480 --> 00:35:54.080
possibility of another explosion.

00:35:54.080 --> 00:35:56.906
I think he
said, "another bomb."

00:35:56.906 --> 00:35:58.410
Another bomb, move back.

00:35:58.410 --> 00:36:00.200
- Oh, my god, another bomb.

00:36:00.200 --> 00:36:02.450
- The fire crews and the
various emergency crews

00:36:02.450 --> 00:36:04.970
are trying to get in, but
we keep getting reports

00:36:04.970 --> 00:36:06.683
that there may be other
devices in the area.

00:36:06.683 --> 00:36:10.070
They will use that
trailer, you see the bucket

00:36:10.070 --> 00:36:11.570
on the back there, sort of, this is how

00:36:11.570 --> 00:36:13.300
they would transport the explosive device

00:36:13.300 --> 00:36:15.040
away from this populated area to try

00:36:15.040 --> 00:36:16.300
to do something with it.

00:36:16.300 --> 00:36:20.420
- There were two unexploded devices

00:36:20.420 --> 00:36:23.380
discovered subsequently
in the initial explosion.

00:36:23.380 --> 00:36:26.610
A second bomb was
found on the east side

00:36:26.610 --> 00:36:29.050
of that building, a bomb
squad is on the scene.

00:36:29.050 --> 00:36:31.160
That second bomb has not exploded.

00:36:31.160 --> 00:36:32.760
We don't know quite the status yet.

00:36:32.760 --> 00:36:35.470
If they've managed to diffuse
it, but it has been confirmed.

00:36:35.470 --> 00:36:39.441
- There have been reports
of two explosive devices,

00:36:39.441 --> 00:36:41.980
unexploded explosive devices.

00:36:41.980 --> 00:36:44.199
Two different
explosive devices were found

00:36:44.199 --> 00:36:46.510
in addition to the one that went off.

00:36:46.510 --> 00:36:48.860
Just an hour after
the initial explosion,

00:36:48.860 --> 00:36:51.540
downtown Oklahoma city
was shaken up again,

00:36:51.540 --> 00:36:54.028
with word of another bomb, or maybe two.

00:36:56.440 --> 00:36:57.950
- They've had to back off a couple times,

00:36:57.950 --> 00:37:00.700
'cause they found, I guess,

00:37:00.700 --> 00:37:01.880
two or three other bombs

00:37:01.880 --> 00:37:03.520
or at least explosive devices down there

00:37:03.520 --> 00:37:05.840
that they've had to diffuse.

00:37:05.840 --> 00:37:08.870
- They shut down operation
for about 20, 30 minutes

00:37:08.870 --> 00:37:12.160
because of that, and
that was very frustrating

00:37:12.160 --> 00:37:14.090
'cause we were right at the point

00:37:14.090 --> 00:37:15.377
where we had people and
we had to leave 'em.

00:37:15.377 --> 00:37:18.190
The first bomb that
was in the federal building

00:37:18.190 --> 00:37:19.740
did go off, it did the damage

00:37:19.740 --> 00:37:21.050
that you see right there.

00:37:21.050 --> 00:37:24.760
The second explosive
was found and diffused.

00:37:24.760 --> 00:37:26.920
- The Oklahoma city bombing
was one of the first

00:37:26.920 --> 00:37:28.450
big stories that I covered,

00:37:28.450 --> 00:37:31.550
and it was just shocking to
know it was an inside job,

00:37:31.550 --> 00:37:34.460
to know that the media was
involved in the cover-up.

00:37:34.460 --> 00:37:38.320
And that the mainstream
television stations

00:37:38.320 --> 00:37:41.790
there in Oklahoma city, knew
what had really happened,

00:37:41.790 --> 00:37:43.690
and then years later,
I was able to actually

00:37:43.690 --> 00:37:45.190
talk to some of those reporters,

00:37:45.190 --> 00:37:47.020
and they discussed how
they were told to shut up.

00:37:47.020 --> 00:37:50.070
I mean, it just showed
how people were so willing

00:37:50.070 --> 00:37:52.340
to be part of the cover-up just because

00:37:52.340 --> 00:37:53.970
the truth was so frightening.

00:37:53.970 --> 00:37:56.330
And that's really why
we've become so enslaved,

00:37:56.330 --> 00:37:58.640
is that we just give in to the lies,

00:37:58.640 --> 00:38:01.560
and they start little, but
they get bigger and bigger.

00:38:01.560 --> 00:38:05.060
- It's amazing when everyone
who can see an event

00:38:05.060 --> 00:38:08.090
and that gets changed into something else,

00:38:08.090 --> 00:38:11.680
simply because the media
presents it that way.

00:38:11.680 --> 00:38:14.040
That means the media's
complicit in the cover-up.

00:38:14.040 --> 00:38:15.350
They're not hapless.

00:38:15.350 --> 00:38:16.580
They're not ignorant.

00:38:16.580 --> 00:38:19.310
How come I can figure
this out and CNN can't?

00:38:19.310 --> 00:38:22.590
- The controlled corporate
mainstream media is essential

00:38:22.590 --> 00:38:24.270
to a cover-up like Oklahoma city

00:38:24.270 --> 00:38:25.940
being successful, and that's why

00:38:25.940 --> 00:38:28.450
the mainstream media has
lost so much credibility.

00:38:28.450 --> 00:38:29.870
Because all over the nation,

00:38:29.870 --> 00:38:31.770
people have seen things like Oklahoma city

00:38:31.770 --> 00:38:34.240
over and over again, where
you see the live footage,

00:38:34.240 --> 00:38:35.680
you see them removing the bombs,

00:38:35.680 --> 00:38:37.407
you see the governor admitting it,

00:38:37.407 --> 00:38:39.947
and then later, the media
says, "we never said that.

00:38:39.947 --> 00:38:42.690
That's what conspiracy theorists say."

00:38:42.690 --> 00:38:44.700
At first, the
media reported on some of these

00:38:44.700 --> 00:38:46.107
bothersome pieces of evidence,

00:38:46.107 --> 00:38:48.060
but they became little more than parrots

00:38:48.060 --> 00:38:50.600
for the justice department
as the official story

00:38:50.600 --> 00:38:53.340
was railroaded into the public mind.

00:38:53.340 --> 00:38:54.540
- Been listening to Mike mccurry,

00:38:54.540 --> 00:38:56.560
President Clinton spokesperson
at the white house.

00:38:56.560 --> 00:38:57.850
Apparently, at this point,
we know a little bit more

00:38:57.850 --> 00:38:59.580
than the white house does
because we have been able

00:38:59.580 --> 00:39:01.520
to confirm that it was a car explosion.

00:39:01.520 --> 00:39:03.770
Now that word coming to us
from mayor Ron norick earlier,

00:39:03.770 --> 00:39:05.950
1,200 pounds of explosives parked out

00:39:05.950 --> 00:39:07.257
in front of the federal building.

00:39:07.257 --> 00:39:10.170
And atf has
confirmed that as well.

00:39:10.170 --> 00:39:12.623
- Who's going to investigate
the investigators?

00:39:13.890 --> 00:39:16.840
Who's going to investigate
the prosecutors?

00:39:16.840 --> 00:39:18.740
Who's gonna hold them accountable?

00:39:18.740 --> 00:39:21.349
Who's gonna hold us public
officials accountable?

00:39:21.349 --> 00:39:22.690
And that's all we're trying to do here

00:39:22.690 --> 00:39:23.943
among trying, in addition to trying

00:39:23.943 --> 00:39:25.690
to find the truth.

00:39:25.690 --> 00:39:28.216
- Well, initially, that morning,

00:39:28.216 --> 00:39:31.460
all the media that was
downtown there reporting

00:39:31.460 --> 00:39:32.993
were reporting the truth.

00:39:34.170 --> 00:39:37.994
They reported the truth
about the unexploded bombs,

00:39:37.994 --> 00:39:41.910
undetonated bombs being
removed from the building.

00:39:41.910 --> 00:39:46.610
By afternoon, things began
to ease a little bit,

00:39:46.610 --> 00:39:48.810
they're just, you could sense a difference

00:39:48.810 --> 00:39:52.572
and by the next day,
everybody but channel 4

00:39:52.572 --> 00:39:55.080
had changed their story completely.

00:39:55.080 --> 00:39:57.980
One local station
in Oklahoma city, kfor-TV,

00:39:57.980 --> 00:40:01.370
did perform its duty by
reporting McVeigh's accomplices,

00:40:01.370 --> 00:40:03.140
the evidence of prior warnings,

00:40:03.140 --> 00:40:05.720
and many other aspects of the case.

00:40:05.720 --> 00:40:07.620
The New York times broadcasting company

00:40:07.620 --> 00:40:10.800
purchased kfor a year after the bombing.

00:40:10.800 --> 00:40:12.850
The programming director was fired,

00:40:12.850 --> 00:40:14.880
the lead journalist on
the bombing, jayna Davis,

00:40:14.880 --> 00:40:16.860
was let go, and all reporting

00:40:16.860 --> 00:40:19.093
that contradicted the
government, banished.

00:40:22.000 --> 00:40:23.410
The victims turned to the government

00:40:23.410 --> 00:40:25.440
with their questions,
expecting the full truth

00:40:25.440 --> 00:40:26.700
to come out.

00:40:26.700 --> 00:40:28.630
This was not to be.

00:40:28.630 --> 00:40:31.430
Those who asked too many
questions or knew too much

00:40:31.430 --> 00:40:34.510
were discouraged from their
efforts in other ways.

00:40:34.510 --> 00:40:37.850
- Debbie nakanashi, who
was with the post office,

00:40:37.850 --> 00:40:42.850
she was told not to talk
to anybody about that.

00:40:43.000 --> 00:40:44.580
Her job had been threatened to her,

00:40:44.580 --> 00:40:46.183
she went to the union over it.

00:40:47.180 --> 00:40:50.410
Then they apologized, but she and I went

00:40:50.410 --> 00:40:53.900
on a number of occasions
to Washington, D.C.

00:40:53.900 --> 00:40:58.400
We tried to see every senator

00:40:58.400 --> 00:41:01.920
and every congressman from Oklahoma.

00:41:01.920 --> 00:41:05.920
Not one would give us an interview.

00:41:05.920 --> 00:41:08.520
- I was told by an agent, an FBI agent,

00:41:08.520 --> 00:41:12.253
that the comments that I'd made, that,

00:41:13.750 --> 00:41:15.707
people like me often ended up dead,

00:41:15.707 --> 00:41:17.817
and be careful what I said

00:41:18.781 --> 00:41:19.864
if I was him.

00:41:21.967 --> 00:41:24.290
In the way that he put it forth,

00:41:24.290 --> 00:41:25.650
I felt like it was a threat.

00:41:25.650 --> 00:41:28.760
- I wrote letters to Janet Reno

00:41:28.760 --> 00:41:32.140
when she was the united
states Attorney General.

00:41:32.140 --> 00:41:34.890
I wrote Louis freeh, was was over the FBI

00:41:34.890 --> 00:41:38.330
at that time, I wrote senator orrin hatch.

00:41:38.330 --> 00:41:40.657
I wrote everybody I could think of

00:41:40.657 --> 00:41:42.260
askin' for help.

00:41:42.260 --> 00:41:43.480
Nothin' was done.

00:41:49.760 --> 00:41:51.730
When the government decided
that the investigation

00:41:51.730 --> 00:41:54.160
was over, a federal
grand jury was impaneled

00:41:54.160 --> 00:41:55.840
to hand down indictments.

00:41:55.840 --> 00:41:58.510
This is usually a straightforward process.

00:41:58.510 --> 00:42:00.760
But the federal prosecutors
were not counting on

00:42:00.760 --> 00:42:02.680
one grand juror, hoppy Heidelberg,

00:42:02.680 --> 00:42:04.643
to actually ask questions of his own.

00:42:05.730 --> 00:42:08.220
- My name is hoppy
Heidelberg and I served on

00:42:08.220 --> 00:42:10.100
the federal grand jury that was supposed

00:42:10.100 --> 00:42:12.260
to investigate the murrah building bombing

00:42:12.260 --> 00:42:15.330
in Oklahoma city back in 1995.

00:42:15.330 --> 00:42:19.480
Actually, the grand jury
has two responsibilities

00:42:20.657 --> 00:42:22.340
that are outlined in this book.

00:42:22.340 --> 00:42:26.070
The first one says,
"the grand jury operates

00:42:26.070 --> 00:42:28.880
as a sword, authorizing the
government for prosecution

00:42:28.880 --> 00:42:31.500
of suspected criminals
and also as a shield,

00:42:31.500 --> 00:42:33.260
protecting citizens from unwanted

00:42:33.260 --> 00:42:35.260
or inappropriate prosecutions."

00:42:35.260 --> 00:42:37.460
That's not somethin' the
media or the government

00:42:37.460 --> 00:42:40.330
ever points out, but that was actually

00:42:40.330 --> 00:42:42.930
the reason for a grand
jury in the first place,

00:42:42.930 --> 00:42:45.330
to protect citizens from the crown,

00:42:45.330 --> 00:42:47.750
who at the time had the habit of

00:42:47.750 --> 00:42:49.900
prosecuting their political enemies

00:42:49.900 --> 00:42:52.823
or anybody they chose for any reason.

00:42:52.823 --> 00:42:54.170
The grand jury, our grand jury

00:42:54.170 --> 00:42:58.480
that was supposed to be calling witnesses,

00:42:58.480 --> 00:43:00.900
were not allowed to call any.

00:43:00.900 --> 00:43:03.220
And it was my letter to the judge,

00:43:03.220 --> 00:43:05.450
tellin' him that and demandin' that we be

00:43:05.450 --> 00:43:07.380
allowed to call witnesses,
that got me excused

00:43:07.380 --> 00:43:08.850
from the grand jury.

00:43:08.850 --> 00:43:11.980
What you will hear and
what they say that's a lie

00:43:11.980 --> 00:43:14.010
is that the grand jury foreman

00:43:15.270 --> 00:43:16.460
is the only one that has the right

00:43:16.460 --> 00:43:17.660
to do this or that.

00:43:17.660 --> 00:43:19.700
And that's not true,
according to the book.

00:43:19.700 --> 00:43:23.760
Any member can demand anything he wants,

00:43:23.760 --> 00:43:24.960
for any reason.

00:43:24.960 --> 00:43:26.710
Can be just his personal opinion,

00:43:26.710 --> 00:43:28.583
it can be from information he gets.

00:43:29.421 --> 00:43:30.737
And of course, they tell us,

00:43:30.737 --> 00:43:32.620
"you can't watch TV.

00:43:32.620 --> 00:43:35.000
You can't read the
paper," that's nonsense.

00:43:35.000 --> 00:43:35.963
That's nonsense.

00:43:37.210 --> 00:43:40.020
Grand jurors need to be well-informed

00:43:40.900 --> 00:43:43.170
if they're gonna do their job properly.

00:43:43.170 --> 00:43:47.200
See, we were never allowed
to see the photo evidence

00:43:47.200 --> 00:43:48.593
from the cameras on the murrah building

00:43:48.593 --> 00:43:52.800
that would have shown
the truck being parked

00:43:53.750 --> 00:43:56.870
and the people who got out of the truck,

00:43:56.870 --> 00:43:57.963
that's all on tape.

00:43:59.520 --> 00:44:01.963
And we were authorized to see all of that,

00:44:02.930 --> 00:44:04.680
but we weren't allowed to see it.

00:44:04.680 --> 00:44:06.570
And in fact, nobody's
been allowed to see it.

00:44:06.570 --> 00:44:08.370
All those tapes have been kept under wraps

00:44:08.370 --> 00:44:10.220
for 15 years.

00:44:10.220 --> 00:44:12.290
It was just too important.

00:44:12.290 --> 00:44:14.730
Just too important to the American people

00:44:14.730 --> 00:44:18.560
to know what happened
there for me to keep quiet.

00:44:18.560 --> 00:44:21.098
Because nobody else was gonna speak up.

00:44:21.098 --> 00:44:23.620
The other grand jurors were petrified

00:44:23.620 --> 00:44:26.011
because they observed on a daily basis

00:44:26.011 --> 00:44:29.830
the kind of intimidation
tactics that were used

00:44:30.770 --> 00:44:32.440
by the department of justice attorneys

00:44:32.440 --> 00:44:34.863
to attempt to keep me under control.

00:44:35.945 --> 00:44:38.640
And when they found out
about the FBI visits

00:44:38.640 --> 00:44:42.200
to my home, that really shook 'em up.

00:44:42.200 --> 00:44:43.400
Now they seem scared to talk to me

00:44:43.400 --> 00:44:44.313
in the men's room.

00:44:45.400 --> 00:44:47.070
Hoppy will never be silenced.

00:44:47.070 --> 00:44:50.040
In 1998, he ran as an
independent candidate

00:44:50.040 --> 00:44:52.740
for governor of Oklahoma,
intent on reopening

00:44:52.740 --> 00:44:55.100
the investigation into the bombing.

00:44:55.100 --> 00:44:57.970
After being excluded from
the gubernatorial debate,

00:44:57.970 --> 00:44:59.740
hoppy walked on stage to ask

00:44:59.740 --> 00:45:01.940
governor frank keating why.

00:45:01.940 --> 00:45:03.270
I'll go up there
on the record as saying,

00:45:03.270 --> 00:45:04.936
do you think I should participate.

00:45:04.936 --> 00:45:06.853
You still believe that?

00:45:16.970 --> 00:45:18.550
- Thank you, audience.

00:45:18.550 --> 00:45:21.003
Mr. Jenkins, your follow-up now.

00:45:27.140 --> 00:45:28.490
Two years after the bombing,

00:45:28.490 --> 00:45:31.600
the trial of Tim McVeigh
began in Denver, Colorado.

00:45:31.600 --> 00:45:33.570
The trial had been moved out of Oklahoma

00:45:33.570 --> 00:45:35.260
despite the constitutional mandate

00:45:35.260 --> 00:45:37.510
that federal crimes must be tried

00:45:37.510 --> 00:45:39.762
in the district in which they occurred.

00:45:39.762 --> 00:45:41.540
The truth seekers were assured that

00:45:41.540 --> 00:45:44.770
all of their questions
would be answered in court.

00:45:44.770 --> 00:45:46.950
- The trial was not handled appropriately,

00:45:46.950 --> 00:45:49.660
it was handled in a way
that was very prejudiced

00:45:49.660 --> 00:45:52.200
against the defendants.

00:45:52.200 --> 00:45:54.910
If you look at what judge matsch did

00:45:54.910 --> 00:45:58.800
concerning prejudicing the jury,

00:45:58.800 --> 00:46:00.920
toward the people that
are being prosecuted by,

00:46:00.920 --> 00:46:03.600
two weeks, he showed them
pictures of dead babies

00:46:03.600 --> 00:46:08.130
and blood and guts, and
which is all basically,

00:46:08.130 --> 00:46:09.940
in my understanding of the law, illegal

00:46:09.940 --> 00:46:11.800
to prejudice the jury like that.

00:46:11.800 --> 00:46:13.730
Yet, they did that kind of stuff,

00:46:13.730 --> 00:46:15.260
apparently on purpose.

00:46:15.260 --> 00:46:18.910
- I was told that by the U.S. attorney

00:46:18.910 --> 00:46:22.643
that if I attended the trials in Denver,

00:46:23.810 --> 00:46:27.433
that all of my questions
would be answered.

00:46:28.760 --> 00:46:31.900
I gave up everything I had,

00:46:31.900 --> 00:46:33.820
my apartment and everything,

00:46:33.820 --> 00:46:35.713
and I moved to Denver.

00:46:37.150 --> 00:46:39.810
And I attended both trials and by the time

00:46:39.810 --> 00:46:41.420
Terry Nichols's trial was over,

00:46:41.420 --> 00:46:43.233
I had more questions.

00:46:45.910 --> 00:46:47.890
And no answers.

00:46:47.890 --> 00:46:49.800
The trial lasted three weeks.

00:46:49.800 --> 00:46:53.410
In contrast, the o.J.
Simpson trial in 1995

00:46:53.410 --> 00:46:55.500
had lasted nine months.

00:46:55.500 --> 00:46:58.060
The jury deliberated
for less than 24 hours,

00:46:58.060 --> 00:47:00.233
and sentenced Tim McVeigh to death.

00:47:01.110 --> 00:47:03.220
McVeigh waived all his appeals,

00:47:03.220 --> 00:47:04.760
and was fast-tracked to be the first

00:47:04.760 --> 00:47:07.810
federal prisoner executed in decades.

00:47:07.810 --> 00:47:09.770
Just before his execution date,

00:47:09.770 --> 00:47:11.850
the FBI announced that they had withheld

00:47:11.850 --> 00:47:13.433
thousands of pages of documents

00:47:13.433 --> 00:47:15.930
that could have influenced his trial,

00:47:15.930 --> 00:47:18.750
which led to a month-long
stay of execution.

00:47:18.750 --> 00:47:21.047
- I mean, they weren't
able to get thousands,

00:47:21.047 --> 00:47:23.880
at least thousands, probably
a lot more than that,

00:47:23.880 --> 00:47:26.110
of documents from, you know, the FBI

00:47:26.110 --> 00:47:27.360
and the DOJ.

00:47:27.360 --> 00:47:29.407
They just wouldn't turn them over.

00:47:29.407 --> 00:47:32.730
On June 11, 2001,
Tim McVeigh was put to death

00:47:32.730 --> 00:47:35.300
by lethal injection at
the federal death row

00:47:35.300 --> 00:47:37.030
in terre haute, Indiana.

00:47:37.030 --> 00:47:39.621
He left no message and
was quickly cremated

00:47:39.621 --> 00:47:42.610
without an autopsy being
performed on his body,

00:47:42.610 --> 00:47:44.420
contrary to the standard procedure

00:47:44.420 --> 00:47:45.833
for executed prisoners.

00:47:47.740 --> 00:47:49.670
Terry Nichols was tried and found guilty

00:47:49.670 --> 00:47:52.030
in a separate trial, and
received a life sentence

00:47:52.030 --> 00:47:53.823
without the possibility of parole.

00:47:54.660 --> 00:47:58.000
In 2004, Terry Nichols
was then tried in Oklahoma

00:47:58.000 --> 00:48:00.560
on state murder charges
in the prosecutors' hope

00:48:00.560 --> 00:48:02.770
of imposing a death sentence.

00:48:02.770 --> 00:48:05.420
Nichols was found guilty,
but a jury once again

00:48:05.420 --> 00:48:07.700
refused to execute him.

00:48:07.700 --> 00:48:09.700
- Those jurors did the best job they could

00:48:09.700 --> 00:48:12.180
with the case that was presented to them.

00:48:12.180 --> 00:48:14.100
I think what their
statement says is they knew

00:48:14.100 --> 00:48:15.550
there was something wrong and somebody

00:48:15.550 --> 00:48:16.930
had some involvement here.

00:48:16.930 --> 00:48:19.231
They also, as they have said themselves,

00:48:19.231 --> 00:48:22.780
that there were lies,
there were mistruths,

00:48:22.780 --> 00:48:25.220
there were bungling, there was arrogance,

00:48:25.220 --> 00:48:27.420
there was things that were not pursued,

00:48:27.420 --> 00:48:30.330
like the other John does,
and so they felt like

00:48:30.330 --> 00:48:31.900
there was a reasonable doubt.

00:48:31.900 --> 00:48:33.500
Michael
fortier became a witness

00:48:33.500 --> 00:48:36.418
for the federal prosecutors,
received a 10-year sentence,

00:48:36.418 --> 00:48:39.380
and was released in 2006 directly into

00:48:39.380 --> 00:48:42.040
the witness protection program.

00:48:42.040 --> 00:48:43.900
Justice, the government announced,

00:48:43.900 --> 00:48:44.977
had been served.

00:48:55.199 --> 00:48:59.013
♪ And I know tomorrow ♪

00:48:59.013 --> 00:49:00.074
Hey!

00:49:00.074 --> 00:49:02.833
♪ Will be the same ♪

00:49:02.833 --> 00:49:07.432
♪ 'cause we've got a life of love ♪

00:49:07.432 --> 00:49:10.657
♪ that won't ever change ♪

00:49:10.657 --> 00:49:12.974
♪ every day ♪

00:49:19.150 --> 00:49:21.200
As the
government proclaimed justice

00:49:21.200 --> 00:49:23.180
for all impacted by the bombing,

00:49:23.180 --> 00:49:26.110
the people back in Oklahoma
still sought the truth,

00:49:26.110 --> 00:49:29.080
and knew now they were on their own.

00:49:29.080 --> 00:49:31.380
The list of questions continued to grow,

00:49:31.380 --> 00:49:34.930
due to the mysterious death of
Oklahoma city police officer

00:49:34.930 --> 00:49:36.818
sergeant Terrance yeakey.

00:49:36.818 --> 00:49:39.340
Terry yeakey, unlike the rest of Oklahoma,

00:49:39.340 --> 00:49:40.763
may have known too much.

00:49:42.060 --> 00:49:46.340
- Officer yeakey was
just over 30 years old

00:49:46.340 --> 00:49:47.870
at the time of the bombing.

00:49:47.870 --> 00:49:48.780
The morning of the bombing,

00:49:48.780 --> 00:49:50.810
he was issuing a traffic ticket

00:49:50.810 --> 00:49:52.610
near the civic center music hall,

00:49:52.610 --> 00:49:54.570
which is about four blocks to the west of

00:49:54.570 --> 00:49:57.110
where the murrah building sits.

00:49:57.110 --> 00:50:01.130
He dropped the ticket
book, let the woman go,

00:50:01.130 --> 00:50:03.680
and says, "I have to,
obviously, attend other things,"

00:50:03.680 --> 00:50:04.950
he heard the multiple blasts coming

00:50:04.950 --> 00:50:06.190
from the murrah building.

00:50:06.190 --> 00:50:07.980
Sped up there in his
Black and white squad car

00:50:07.980 --> 00:50:09.780
and immediately started
pulling out the first

00:50:09.780 --> 00:50:12.640
of eight people; Mr. Tom
hall being the first,

00:50:12.640 --> 00:50:14.443
a former employee of the gsa.

00:50:15.720 --> 00:50:17.950
Tom, to this day, in fact, I talked to him

00:50:17.950 --> 00:50:20.020
a couple of weeks ago,
still has the utmost respect

00:50:20.020 --> 00:50:20.990
for officer yeakey.

00:50:20.990 --> 00:50:22.970
He literally saved his life.

00:50:22.970 --> 00:50:26.580
Officer yeakey, being
an astute police officer

00:50:26.580 --> 00:50:27.670
for seven years, veteran of

00:50:27.670 --> 00:50:29.900
the Oklahoma city police department,

00:50:29.900 --> 00:50:32.520
knew that something was horribly wrong.

00:50:32.520 --> 00:50:34.610
He tried to get the official storyline out

00:50:34.610 --> 00:50:36.460
through his commanding
officers at the Oklahoma city

00:50:36.460 --> 00:50:37.810
police department, through his family,

00:50:37.810 --> 00:50:39.170
through his ex-wife,

00:50:39.170 --> 00:50:42.470
and he chose to withhold
some of the storyline

00:50:42.470 --> 00:50:45.150
because he was in fear of
for his family and his wife

00:50:45.150 --> 00:50:47.263
and his two young daughters at the time.

00:50:48.218 --> 00:50:50.280
What we found out, between the hours

00:50:50.280 --> 00:50:53.079
of eight A.M. and one P.M. that morning,

00:50:53.079 --> 00:50:55.850
he was brutally murdered a mile and a half

00:50:55.850 --> 00:50:58.890
from the front gate of
the El Reno penitentiary.

00:50:58.890 --> 00:51:02.780
From that moment that his body was found,

00:51:02.780 --> 00:51:04.600
we know that the crime
scene was destroyed.

00:51:04.600 --> 00:51:06.760
There were spade shovels that were used

00:51:06.760 --> 00:51:08.470
to turn over the crime scene,

00:51:08.470 --> 00:51:10.020
ballistics, any gunpowder residue,

00:51:10.020 --> 00:51:11.780
anything that had to do with his death

00:51:11.780 --> 00:51:13.630
was completely destroyed,
it was corrupted.

00:51:13.630 --> 00:51:16.640
- He started having problems
with, not only at work,

00:51:16.640 --> 00:51:18.340
but his apartment got broke into,

00:51:18.340 --> 00:51:20.440
his car got broke into, things were stolen

00:51:20.440 --> 00:51:21.460
out of his house.

00:51:21.460 --> 00:51:24.080
He had accumulated reports, evidence,

00:51:24.080 --> 00:51:26.500
I don't know what all, but
he was going to take it

00:51:26.500 --> 00:51:29.283
out to a mini storage in El Reno.

00:51:30.710 --> 00:51:34.270
And he left one night,

00:51:34.270 --> 00:51:35.860
and he told a friend of his

00:51:35.860 --> 00:51:37.180
that they were gonna go out to dinner,

00:51:37.180 --> 00:51:38.930
he says, "I gotta run
out and put some stuff

00:51:38.930 --> 00:51:40.998
in mini storage and soon as I shake

00:51:40.998 --> 00:51:43.670
these feds that are followin' me,

00:51:43.670 --> 00:51:45.440
I'll be back and we'll go to dinner."

00:51:45.440 --> 00:51:47.350
He never came back

00:51:47.350 --> 00:51:48.770
instead, he was found the next day

00:51:48.770 --> 00:51:51.260
by Canadian county sheriff's deputy.

00:51:51.260 --> 00:51:52.197
Well, they found his car first,

00:51:52.197 --> 00:51:54.280
and then they found him in a field

00:51:54.280 --> 00:51:55.863
near the El Reno penitentiary.

00:51:56.720 --> 00:52:00.763
The damage to his body was
obviously a torture homicide.

00:52:01.640 --> 00:52:03.060
It was obvious.

00:52:03.060 --> 00:52:05.570
But what intrigued me the most

00:52:05.570 --> 00:52:07.820
that he had several cuts
on both of his wrists,

00:52:07.820 --> 00:52:11.730
inside both elbows, both jugular veins.

00:52:11.730 --> 00:52:13.315
He'd been beaten.

00:52:13.315 --> 00:52:16.030
He had ligature marks around his neck,

00:52:16.030 --> 00:52:18.650
he had handcuff marks on his hands,

00:52:18.650 --> 00:52:21.700
on his wrists, and he had a small caliber

00:52:22.908 --> 00:52:25.373
bullet wound that started above

00:52:25.373 --> 00:52:28.740
on the right-hand side of his temple,

00:52:28.740 --> 00:52:32.160
and exited low on his cheek,

00:52:32.160 --> 00:52:33.950
with no powder burns.

00:52:33.950 --> 00:52:37.040
- The day of his death,
when my daughter called me,

00:52:37.040 --> 00:52:39.530
I left work, went to El Reno

00:52:40.597 --> 00:52:45.597
to help because I could hear
the seriousness in her voice

00:52:45.890 --> 00:52:48.010
that she was getting
upset, why would the police

00:52:48.010 --> 00:52:50.980
be callin' her lookin' for Terrance?

00:52:50.980 --> 00:52:53.350
And when we went to the apartment

00:52:53.350 --> 00:52:58.097
where he lived, the
manager there stated to us,

00:52:58.097 --> 00:53:00.200
"well, why are you lookin'
for him, the police

00:53:00.200 --> 00:53:03.480
have already been here
and taken his cruiser."

00:53:03.480 --> 00:53:06.260
I'm not sure what was goin' on,

00:53:06.260 --> 00:53:07.760
it was strange.

00:53:07.760 --> 00:53:09.943
At about 10 o'clock at night,

00:53:11.030 --> 00:53:13.453
I had put my grandkids to bed.

00:53:15.170 --> 00:53:18.750
The phone rang, and when
I picked the phone up,

00:53:18.750 --> 00:53:21.400
I could hear my daughter
screamin' in the background.

00:53:22.520 --> 00:53:25.600
And I assumed something bad had happened,

00:53:25.600 --> 00:53:27.393
but I didn't think death.

00:53:28.800 --> 00:53:31.580
And my son said, "mom, they found Terry.

00:53:31.580 --> 00:53:32.413
He's dead."

00:53:33.900 --> 00:53:36.460
- One of the things that surprised me was

00:53:36.460 --> 00:53:39.070
that there was no autopsy performed.

00:53:39.070 --> 00:53:41.040
The other thing that
really bothered me was

00:53:41.040 --> 00:53:44.390
we were being told that Terry
was high on drugs and drunk.

00:53:44.390 --> 00:53:47.750
And of course, the
medical examiner's office

00:53:47.750 --> 00:53:51.283
did a report on Terry and his injuries,

00:53:52.300 --> 00:53:53.730
which was really not an autopsy,

00:53:53.730 --> 00:53:58.730
just an overview, and
it showed that his bac

00:53:59.640 --> 00:54:04.560
was zero, meaning no
blood alcohol content.

00:54:04.560 --> 00:54:07.040
There was no drugs in his system.

00:54:07.040 --> 00:54:08.790
It bothered me that
they didn't treat Terry

00:54:08.790 --> 00:54:13.099
like the police officer like he was.

00:54:13.099 --> 00:54:15.890
He was a good guy.

00:54:15.890 --> 00:54:19.447
- And he never said to
us that "I'm depressed."

00:54:21.310 --> 00:54:22.947
You know, "I need help."

00:54:24.330 --> 00:54:28.470
Not to me, or not to his sisters.

00:54:28.470 --> 00:54:31.440
I think it's only fair that we know,

00:54:31.440 --> 00:54:35.145
as Terrence's family
members, what happened.

00:54:35.145 --> 00:54:38.690
- Officer yeakey's official
cause of death was suicide,

00:54:38.690 --> 00:54:40.440
and that was actually laid out

00:54:40.440 --> 00:54:42.260
on the medical examiner's report

00:54:42.260 --> 00:54:43.730
at the Oklahoma state medical office,

00:54:43.730 --> 00:54:45.590
examiner's office.

00:54:45.590 --> 00:54:47.890
We've since were able
to retrieve that record.

00:54:49.220 --> 00:54:51.320
What we found out though
is that number one,

00:54:51.320 --> 00:54:52.870
the crime scene was corrupted,

00:54:52.870 --> 00:54:54.690
went completely in the face

00:54:54.690 --> 00:54:57.450
of proper investigative procedure.

00:54:57.450 --> 00:55:01.500
The extent and the amount,
the number of wounds

00:55:01.500 --> 00:55:04.220
on his body clearly shows that he was,

00:55:04.220 --> 00:55:05.760
he couldn't commit suicide.

00:55:05.760 --> 00:55:08.440
Physically and logistically,
you just can't do that

00:55:08.440 --> 00:55:09.440
to yourself.

00:55:09.440 --> 00:55:11.440
Terry also, we knew, was anemic.

00:55:11.440 --> 00:55:13.060
He would not have been able to traverse

00:55:13.060 --> 00:55:15.430
over half a mile from where his car was

00:55:15.430 --> 00:55:17.200
to where his body was found,

00:55:17.200 --> 00:55:18.920
and not have passed out,
his heart would have

00:55:18.920 --> 00:55:20.240
literally given out, he wouldn't have had

00:55:20.240 --> 00:55:23.439
enough blood pressure
in his body to survive.

00:55:23.439 --> 00:55:26.660
The car was locked, the
windows were rolled up.

00:55:26.660 --> 00:55:28.560
The keys were in the console.

00:55:28.560 --> 00:55:30.793
There was a bloody knife in the glove box.

00:55:31.730 --> 00:55:33.810
You don't stab yourself 13 times

00:55:33.810 --> 00:55:36.273
and have superficial wounds on the,

00:55:37.260 --> 00:55:39.620
along your arms and
chest and your upper neck

00:55:39.620 --> 00:55:42.220
and walk a half a mile and decide to die

00:55:42.220 --> 00:55:43.630
next a tree.

00:55:43.630 --> 00:55:46.473
- Being the family of an officer,

00:55:48.317 --> 00:55:51.840
I expected some kind of care

00:55:51.840 --> 00:55:55.130
and consideration for us,

00:55:55.130 --> 00:55:57.030
being the family of Terrance.

00:55:57.030 --> 00:56:01.010
There was another detective
by the name of mullinex

00:56:01.010 --> 00:56:04.160
that told my daughter that she looked at

00:56:04.160 --> 00:56:06.270
too many movies and she needed to see

00:56:06.270 --> 00:56:10.330
a psychiatrist, when we
were asking questions,

00:56:10.330 --> 00:56:13.110
wanting to know about his belongings,

00:56:13.110 --> 00:56:15.660
wanting to know about things that happened

00:56:15.660 --> 00:56:17.830
during the course of where they say

00:56:17.830 --> 00:56:20.900
they found my son.

00:56:20.900 --> 00:56:24.810
And I don't think this
was very kind of them

00:56:24.810 --> 00:56:27.063
and considerate of us, being family,

00:56:28.380 --> 00:56:30.630
that they should have
talked to us like that.

00:56:31.930 --> 00:56:32.763
But they did.

00:56:33.780 --> 00:56:37.740
And as far as I'm concerned,
that made me more suspicious

00:56:37.740 --> 00:56:39.223
of what happened to my son.

00:56:40.480 --> 00:56:42.930
The brutal torture
and murder of Terry yeakey

00:56:42.930 --> 00:56:45.380
served not only to silence his voice,

00:56:45.380 --> 00:56:47.460
but the voices of other first responders,

00:56:47.460 --> 00:56:49.390
who may have seen something
that would shed light

00:56:49.390 --> 00:56:50.593
on what really happened.

00:56:51.650 --> 00:56:55.610
Those who keep their silence
know exactly what Terry saw.

00:56:55.610 --> 00:56:57.120
But he will never be forgotten

00:56:57.120 --> 00:56:59.833
by those who ask questions
and demand answers.

00:57:09.780 --> 00:57:12.060
In the absence of official action,

00:57:12.060 --> 00:57:14.500
a group of concerned
citizens decided to form

00:57:14.500 --> 00:57:16.510
their own investigative panel:

00:57:16.510 --> 00:57:18.970
The okbic, better known as

00:57:18.970 --> 00:57:21.223
the Oklahoma bombing
investigation committee.

00:57:22.380 --> 00:57:24.560
Their goal was to compile enough evidence

00:57:24.560 --> 00:57:26.350
that would attract attention by the media

00:57:26.350 --> 00:57:28.460
and the government, and therefore compel

00:57:28.460 --> 00:57:30.373
a more thorough investigation.

00:57:31.280 --> 00:57:34.490
Entirely funded by donations
and their own money,

00:57:34.490 --> 00:57:38.800
the okbic took affidavits,
recorded eyewitness testimony,

00:57:38.800 --> 00:57:40.480
and paid for private investigators

00:57:40.480 --> 00:57:42.490
to chase down leads.

00:57:42.490 --> 00:57:44.855
- I'm Charles key, state representative

00:57:44.855 --> 00:57:47.010
in Oklahoma city, and I've formed

00:57:47.010 --> 00:57:49.040
the Oklahoma bombing
investigation committee.

00:57:49.040 --> 00:57:52.230
I had a number of constituents come to me

00:57:52.230 --> 00:57:55.070
and other people that started raising

00:57:55.070 --> 00:57:59.050
their own questions
about the investigation,

00:57:59.050 --> 00:58:00.200
what direction it was goin',

00:58:00.200 --> 00:58:02.780
because it seemed like there was an effort

00:58:02.780 --> 00:58:06.994
to try to change that initial report

00:58:06.994 --> 00:58:09.790
of what took place on the
first day of the bombing

00:58:09.790 --> 00:58:11.680
as the days and weeks went by.

00:58:11.680 --> 00:58:12.860
- We looked at what state representative

00:58:12.860 --> 00:58:13.780
Charles key did.

00:58:13.780 --> 00:58:15.440
He went on the facts,

00:58:15.440 --> 00:58:18.040
he went on the information
the grand jury gleaned,

00:58:18.040 --> 00:58:20.480
and clearly there was
complete prior knowledge.

00:58:20.480 --> 00:58:24.480
- I observed the fact that Charles key

00:58:25.850 --> 00:58:30.760
seemed to be standing up for

00:58:30.760 --> 00:58:32.910
the truth in some areas that I felt like

00:58:34.070 --> 00:58:35.860
was not being dealt with appropriately

00:58:35.860 --> 00:58:37.480
by authorities.

00:58:37.480 --> 00:58:39.270
The Oklahoma bombing
investigation committee

00:58:39.270 --> 00:58:42.810
was formed for one purpose and
that is to obtain the truth.

00:58:42.810 --> 00:58:45.060
- First, I thought, "ah,
that's just another politician

00:58:45.060 --> 00:58:47.603
trying to get a little publicity,"

00:58:48.830 --> 00:58:52.280
then when I met them, met Charles key

00:58:52.280 --> 00:58:57.280
and colonel Wallace, and Dale Phillips,

00:58:57.950 --> 00:59:00.250
found out that they were for real,

00:59:00.250 --> 00:59:03.746
and they asked me if I would join 'em.

00:59:03.746 --> 00:59:05.890
And I agreed to join 'em.

00:59:05.890 --> 00:59:09.170
- I think Charles key's work
is absolutely outstanding,

00:59:09.170 --> 00:59:10.530
and it continues to be.

00:59:10.530 --> 00:59:11.640
Even to this day, we're looking at

00:59:11.640 --> 00:59:15.130
about 16 years on,
almost, coming this April,

00:59:15.130 --> 00:59:16.740
Charles took a lot of risks.

00:59:16.740 --> 00:59:19.707
- When we saw what was goin'
on with the investigation,

00:59:19.707 --> 00:59:23.500
and that it was trying to move away from

00:59:23.500 --> 00:59:25.210
the early facts that were presented

00:59:25.210 --> 00:59:27.780
by law enforcement and by the media,

00:59:27.780 --> 00:59:30.810
we pursued establishing
a county grand jury

00:59:30.810 --> 00:59:32.170
in Oklahoma county.

00:59:32.170 --> 00:59:33.730
Something unique to Oklahoma

00:59:33.730 --> 00:59:36.490
and just a few other states in the country

00:59:36.490 --> 00:59:38.730
that allow citizens' grand juries

00:59:38.730 --> 00:59:41.840
to be impaneled to investigate
things such as this.

00:59:41.840 --> 00:59:46.600
- The committee meetings
were very serious.

00:59:46.600 --> 00:59:49.540
We fought the government at every level,

00:59:49.540 --> 00:59:52.400
all the way through to the supreme court

00:59:52.400 --> 00:59:53.810
of the state.

00:59:53.810 --> 00:59:55.537
- We had a lot of people that came forward

00:59:55.537 --> 00:59:57.210
and brought us a lot of information

00:59:57.210 --> 00:59:59.030
that we wouldn't have
gotten any other way.

00:59:59.030 --> 01:00:02.280
We were pursuing all the information

01:00:02.280 --> 01:00:03.897
that we could get our hands on

01:00:03.897 --> 01:00:05.640
about the bombing,

01:00:05.640 --> 01:00:07.940
and we were trying to get a
congressional investigation

01:00:07.940 --> 01:00:09.240
of the bombing.

01:00:09.240 --> 01:00:10.707
- I was in awe at the amount of effort

01:00:10.707 --> 01:00:12.143
that they put in in that first

01:00:12.143 --> 01:00:14.680
six and a half years before
the book was released,

01:00:14.680 --> 01:00:15.750
and then they have the book released,

01:00:15.750 --> 01:00:17.540
come out to the general public

01:00:17.540 --> 01:00:19.830
three weeks before 9/11 occurred.

01:00:19.830 --> 01:00:22.170
And to see every single
obstacle that was thrown

01:00:22.170 --> 01:00:24.670
in their face from, all
the way from the news media

01:00:24.670 --> 01:00:27.880
to financial, to emotional,

01:00:27.880 --> 01:00:31.920
and interviewing over 329
victims, family members,

01:00:31.920 --> 01:00:33.200
and survivors, all these people

01:00:33.200 --> 01:00:35.807
were consistently, basically saying,

01:00:35.807 --> 01:00:37.940
"I am not going to fail,
I'm not gonna quit,

01:00:37.940 --> 01:00:40.060
I want the truth to come out on this."

01:00:40.060 --> 01:00:42.937
- So we formed the
Oklahoma county grand jury

01:00:42.937 --> 01:00:46.840
to have essentially a
citizens' investigation

01:00:46.840 --> 01:00:49.520
into the Oklahoma bombing,

01:00:49.520 --> 01:00:53.760
and that caused us to have to get,

01:00:53.760 --> 01:00:55.580
to gather a number of signatures

01:00:55.580 --> 01:00:56.880
from citizens of Oklahoma county,

01:00:56.880 --> 01:00:57.910
which we did.

01:00:57.910 --> 01:00:59.510
- We got, I don't know,

01:00:59.510 --> 01:01:00.900
11, 12,000 signatures.

01:01:00.900 --> 01:01:02.763
We only required 5,000.

01:01:03.835 --> 01:01:06.720
And by getting all those signatures,

01:01:06.720 --> 01:01:08.050
getting them validated and everything,

01:01:08.050 --> 01:01:10.940
we then got x amount of
money, a lot of money,

01:01:10.940 --> 01:01:13.220
and the opportunity to
set up a grand jury.

01:01:13.220 --> 01:01:15.330
Well, they turned the grand jury

01:01:15.330 --> 01:01:17.020
over to our enemy,

01:01:17.020 --> 01:01:19.490
which was Bob Macy,

01:01:19.490 --> 01:01:22.060
and basically gave him the money,

01:01:22.060 --> 01:01:24.370
and then he proceeded to investigate us.

01:01:24.370 --> 01:01:28.590
- I wrote a letter to the
district attorney, Macy.

01:01:28.590 --> 01:01:30.860
Told him what I had seen

01:01:30.860 --> 01:01:34.050
and that I wanted to
testify in the grand jury.

01:01:34.050 --> 01:01:35.770
I got a letter back from him

01:01:35.770 --> 01:01:37.880
telling me that the grand jury

01:01:37.880 --> 01:01:40.480
did not want to hear anything I had to say

01:01:40.480 --> 01:01:41.710
about the bombing.

01:01:41.710 --> 01:01:45.034
- After the Oklahoma county grand jury

01:01:45.034 --> 01:01:48.490
was actually initially formed,

01:01:48.490 --> 01:01:51.012
then there were some
efforts to try to stop that

01:01:51.012 --> 01:01:54.560
by the Oklahoma county da and others.

01:01:54.560 --> 01:01:56.210
And at that time,

01:01:56.210 --> 01:02:00.280
we organized ourself in a more formal way.

01:02:00.280 --> 01:02:03.711
We hired private investigators
and some others to help us

01:02:03.711 --> 01:02:08.100
put the information that we
had gathered together in a form

01:02:08.100 --> 01:02:11.426
that we could present to
that county grand jury.

01:02:11.426 --> 01:02:14.320
- Four or five, six months
into the investigation,

01:02:14.320 --> 01:02:18.175
we started suspecting

01:02:18.175 --> 01:02:20.283
that our phones were tapped,

01:02:21.520 --> 01:02:24.700
and I don't remember how
we got the information,

01:02:24.700 --> 01:02:27.870
but there was, we were given
a number that we could dial

01:02:27.870 --> 01:02:29.663
and it would either confirm or,

01:02:29.663 --> 01:02:32.830
they were tapped or that they weren't.

01:02:32.830 --> 01:02:36.510
And we dialed this number
and it would confirm it.

01:02:36.510 --> 01:02:38.010
We didn't really have anything to hide,

01:02:38.010 --> 01:02:39.980
so it didn't really make
that much difference.

01:02:39.980 --> 01:02:42.570
It didn't affect our
investigation too much.

01:02:42.570 --> 01:02:46.770
- I think as we finalized our
work as we got to the end,

01:02:46.770 --> 01:02:48.290
as that grand jury was impaneled,

01:02:48.290 --> 01:02:51.145
and as we put this report together,

01:02:51.145 --> 01:02:54.500
we had a lot of media that
was waiting for this report.

01:02:54.500 --> 01:02:57.500
They were ready to give it
some significant coverage,

01:02:57.500 --> 01:03:00.500
and our report came back
from the book publisher

01:03:00.500 --> 01:03:04.590
about two weeks before 9/11,

01:03:04.590 --> 01:03:06.047
and one of the things that we said

01:03:06.047 --> 01:03:08.930
and some others said
during that time frame,

01:03:08.930 --> 01:03:11.580
as before and after 9/11,

01:03:11.580 --> 01:03:13.130
that the reason that we did this

01:03:13.130 --> 01:03:15.510
is because if you don't ask the questions

01:03:15.510 --> 01:03:17.560
and you don't hold government accountable

01:03:18.500 --> 01:03:19.720
in everything that it does,

01:03:19.720 --> 01:03:23.230
not just bombings like
this, but everything,

01:03:23.230 --> 01:03:25.500
then you'll have the same
mistakes happen again

01:03:25.500 --> 01:03:27.763
and they will get worse as time goes on.

01:03:34.460 --> 01:03:35.870
The official story dictated

01:03:35.870 --> 01:03:36.770
that the Ryder truck

01:03:36.770 --> 01:03:39.770
packed with 1,200 pounds of
ammonium nitrate fertilizer

01:03:39.770 --> 01:03:41.920
and fuel oil, called anfo,

01:03:41.920 --> 01:03:44.450
detonated on the northeast
side of the building

01:03:44.450 --> 01:03:47.000
and was responsible for all the damage.

01:03:47.000 --> 01:03:51.000
That hypothesis later evolved
into the 4,800 pounds of anfo,

01:03:51.000 --> 01:03:53.590
then up to 7,000 pounds of fertilizer

01:03:53.590 --> 01:03:55.740
and nitromethane?

01:03:55.740 --> 01:03:58.920
In fact, the only consistent
theme of the official narrative

01:03:58.920 --> 01:04:00.403
is its inconsistency.

01:04:01.540 --> 01:04:04.330
- The truck bomb just
delivers an air blast.

01:04:04.330 --> 01:04:06.620
That's all it does, it's
called an air blast.

01:04:06.620 --> 01:04:11.040
But when you've got
eight-foot-thick columns

01:04:11.040 --> 01:04:13.360
of concrete filled with rebar

01:04:13.360 --> 01:04:14.913
the size of your arm,

01:04:16.640 --> 01:04:20.710
an air blast probably
won't even break one.

01:04:20.710 --> 01:04:23.700
It will break windows, that's about it,

01:04:23.700 --> 01:04:26.320
but some of these columns were ripped up,

01:04:26.320 --> 01:04:29.400
shredded, tossed around.

01:04:29.400 --> 01:04:34.100
- Because a truck bomb is
gonna release its energy

01:04:35.720 --> 01:04:39.103
simultaneously in every direction,

01:04:41.090 --> 01:04:44.480
and so the damage pattern to the building

01:04:44.480 --> 01:04:46.563
or whatever structure
it's parked in front of

01:04:46.563 --> 01:04:48.380
and intending to blow
up, if it's a big enough,

01:04:48.380 --> 01:04:50.968
big structure, bigger than
a truck bomb can take out,

01:04:50.968 --> 01:04:53.873
the damage pattern's gonna
be roughly a semicircle.

01:04:54.750 --> 01:04:56.440
- Now, I looked at the building,

01:04:56.440 --> 01:04:58.210
I was on the bomb squad
for a couple of years,

01:04:58.210 --> 01:04:59.760
I've worked some bombings,

01:04:59.760 --> 01:05:01.370
and I looked at the building and I knew

01:05:01.370 --> 01:05:03.413
that the damage done to that building

01:05:03.413 --> 01:05:06.820
couldn't have come from
a truck with anfo in it.

01:05:06.820 --> 01:05:09.863
- A blast does not turn corners,

01:05:12.179 --> 01:05:15.733
and it did look like that
there was a secondary explosion

01:05:15.733 --> 01:05:18.347
or a more intense explosion towards

01:05:20.110 --> 01:05:22.050
the east side of the building.

01:05:22.050 --> 01:05:25.861
The explosion, or that
portion of the explosion

01:05:25.861 --> 01:05:28.682
did basically clear everything

01:05:28.682 --> 01:05:31.960
from the front of the
building to the south wall.

01:05:31.960 --> 01:05:34.210
The Oklahoma
bombing investigation committee

01:05:34.210 --> 01:05:36.810
was presented with evidence
that explosives planted

01:05:36.810 --> 01:05:39.220
inside the building were responsible

01:05:39.220 --> 01:05:41.720
for the collapse and
most of the casualties.

01:05:41.720 --> 01:05:43.160
In this rarely seen footage

01:05:43.160 --> 01:05:45.210
taken by the Oklahoma
county sheriff's office

01:05:45.210 --> 01:05:46.747
minutes after the bombing,

01:05:46.747 --> 01:05:49.080
the north side parking
lot is shown littered

01:05:49.080 --> 01:05:52.350
with paper and debris from
inside the murrah building.

01:05:52.350 --> 01:05:54.610
How did this volume of
paper transport itself

01:05:54.610 --> 01:05:56.960
against the blast wave of the truck bomb

01:05:56.960 --> 01:05:59.610
and magically appear on the
other side of the street?

01:06:00.690 --> 01:06:02.420
- And then we look at the fact

01:06:02.420 --> 01:06:04.480
that you have bombs clearly
inside the building,

01:06:04.480 --> 01:06:05.980
it's blown out across the street,

01:06:05.980 --> 01:06:07.907
pieces of it on top of buildings

01:06:07.907 --> 01:06:11.030
the opposite direction that
the rubble should have,

01:06:11.030 --> 01:06:13.010
you know, gone in if there was truly

01:06:13.010 --> 01:06:15.190
this high-powered truck bomb out front

01:06:15.190 --> 01:06:16.750
that caused all the damage.

01:06:16.750 --> 01:06:18.180
- And I can tell you that
the building was blown

01:06:18.180 --> 01:06:20.603
from the inside because
all the debris was piled up

01:06:20.603 --> 01:06:22.840
against the general electric building

01:06:22.840 --> 01:06:24.360
clear across the parking lot.

01:06:24.360 --> 01:06:26.310
In fact,
several witnesses report

01:06:26.310 --> 01:06:28.410
that bombs were going off in the building

01:06:28.410 --> 01:06:30.539
before the truck bomb exploded outside.

01:06:30.539 --> 01:06:32.543
- The first thing that I experienced,

01:06:32.543 --> 01:06:36.160
when I was sitting there
signin' some papers for Ruth,

01:06:36.160 --> 01:06:38.020
I felt the building start shaking

01:06:38.020 --> 01:06:40.890
and never had anything
like that happen before

01:06:40.890 --> 01:06:43.180
and I just kind of froze,

01:06:43.180 --> 01:06:45.190
and then the lights went out.

01:06:45.190 --> 01:06:48.440
It didn't get totally dark
because the whole front

01:06:48.440 --> 01:06:50.020
of the building was glass.

01:06:50.020 --> 01:06:52.670
The lights went out and then the debris

01:06:52.670 --> 01:06:54.970
started fallin' on my desk,

01:06:54.970 --> 01:06:57.900
and then somethin' hit me
in the back of the head

01:06:57.900 --> 01:07:01.330
and knocked me out before
the truck bomb went off.

01:07:01.330 --> 01:07:02.720
What that tells you is that there were

01:07:02.720 --> 01:07:04.293
other explosive devices in the building

01:07:04.293 --> 01:07:06.680
that actually brought the building down.

01:07:06.680 --> 01:07:11.680
- The building started
to sway back and forth,

01:07:12.740 --> 01:07:14.610
it was going back and forth.

01:07:14.610 --> 01:07:17.587
And I had sat there and I thought,

01:07:17.587 --> 01:07:20.120
"no, it doesn't feel like an earthquake,"

01:07:20.120 --> 01:07:22.250
and I was kind of stunned

01:07:22.250 --> 01:07:27.176
and then about seven
or eight seconds later,

01:07:27.176 --> 01:07:31.420
I felt this explosion, and you could feel,

01:07:31.420 --> 01:07:36.420
actually feel the concrete floor

01:07:36.720 --> 01:07:38.920
actually rising from underneath you.

01:07:38.920 --> 01:07:42.360
You could feel it coming
up from the other side.

01:07:42.360 --> 01:07:43.750
- It was like slow motion.

01:07:43.750 --> 01:07:44.970
We crawled under

01:07:44.970 --> 01:07:46.310
before the glass started coming

01:07:46.310 --> 01:07:47.560
and everything that just,

01:07:48.480 --> 01:07:51.090
it just seemed to,
seemed to roll in on us.

01:07:51.090 --> 01:07:53.989
I thought it was an
earthquake when it started.

01:07:53.989 --> 01:07:55.690
It was just a kind of a shake

01:07:55.690 --> 01:07:57.730
and then everything
started going like this

01:07:57.730 --> 01:08:00.477
and I dove under the desk and
then all the glass came in

01:08:00.477 --> 01:08:02.227
and the ceilings came down and-

01:08:03.460 --> 01:08:04.320
- three seismographs

01:08:04.320 --> 01:08:05.917
at the university of Oklahoma,

01:08:05.917 --> 01:08:08.860
the omniplex science museum,
and in Franklin, Oklahoma,

01:08:08.860 --> 01:08:12.050
recorded a seismic event
lasting eight to 10 seconds

01:08:12.050 --> 01:08:14.920
that "suggest the
possibility of two blasts."

01:08:14.920 --> 01:08:16.860
There were two energetic spikes,

01:08:16.860 --> 01:08:18.910
one was the truck bomb,
and the second spike

01:08:18.910 --> 01:08:20.620
was explained away as air blast

01:08:20.620 --> 01:08:23.490
pushing on the ground or falling debris.

01:08:23.490 --> 01:08:26.330
But a representative of the
Oklahoma geological survey

01:08:26.330 --> 01:08:28.530
stated for the record that this spike

01:08:28.530 --> 01:08:30.800
was not the result of floors collapsing,

01:08:30.800 --> 01:08:32.650
and that the last five
seconds of ground motion

01:08:32.650 --> 01:08:35.333
did not have air blast associated with it.

01:08:42.470 --> 01:08:45.620
The khobar towers bombing
in 1996 in Saudi Arabia

01:08:45.620 --> 01:08:47.570
killed 19 U.S. airmen.

01:08:47.570 --> 01:08:49.930
That bomb was several
times larger than the bombs

01:08:49.930 --> 01:08:52.200
supposed to have been used in Oklahoma.

01:08:52.200 --> 01:08:54.089
It left a huge 85-foot crater,

01:08:54.089 --> 01:08:56.230
yet there was no major structural damage

01:08:56.230 --> 01:08:57.630
on the simple slab building.

01:08:58.890 --> 01:09:00.400
What happened in Oklahoma city

01:09:00.400 --> 01:09:03.310
to cause the major horizontal
support beam to fail

01:09:03.310 --> 01:09:05.880
and the complete failure of
these two series of columns

01:09:05.880 --> 01:09:07.840
on the east side of the building?

01:09:07.840 --> 01:09:11.270
This collapse was responsible
for most of the casualties.

01:09:11.270 --> 01:09:13.460
The crater, when seen from above,

01:09:13.460 --> 01:09:15.510
is offset from the major structural damage

01:09:15.510 --> 01:09:16.740
in the building.

01:09:16.740 --> 01:09:18.690
For some reason, the official story

01:09:18.690 --> 01:09:20.540
has inflated the size of this crater.

01:09:22.640 --> 01:09:25.800
- The bomb, at least I've
seen where the reports

01:09:25.800 --> 01:09:28.980
from the different agencies
have said the bomb extended

01:09:28.980 --> 01:09:31.730
from the cab to the tail of the truck.

01:09:31.730 --> 01:09:35.590
And one other thing that
really bothers me about that is

01:09:35.590 --> 01:09:38.850
is the rear axle on the truck

01:09:38.850 --> 01:09:40.360
went down and collided with a car

01:09:40.360 --> 01:09:41.540
in front of the regency tower

01:09:41.540 --> 01:09:43.040
about a block and a half away.

01:09:43.970 --> 01:09:48.480
The front axle of the
truck was hurled eastbound

01:09:48.480 --> 01:09:52.612
and struck a parking meter
about a block and a half away

01:09:52.612 --> 01:09:54.633
in front of the ymca building.

01:09:54.633 --> 01:09:56.120
If a bomb was that big,
that that rear axle

01:09:56.120 --> 01:09:59.474
would have been driven into the crater

01:09:59.474 --> 01:10:02.953
instead of being split
apart, as they were.

01:10:04.020 --> 01:10:07.170
And the truck bomb itself, to me,

01:10:07.170 --> 01:10:10.240
had to be between the two axles.

01:10:10.240 --> 01:10:12.390
It could not have been
over that real axle.

01:10:12.390 --> 01:10:16.150
- I was surprised from
the, even the fema report

01:10:16.150 --> 01:10:19.540
and the published reports
that nobody could determine

01:10:19.540 --> 01:10:21.110
what the size of the crater was,

01:10:21.110 --> 01:10:22.877
and that's one of the things I brought up

01:10:22.877 --> 01:10:24.470
with the grand jury investigation

01:10:24.470 --> 01:10:26.360
is that the crater was half the size

01:10:26.360 --> 01:10:30.390
that they had proposed in the fema report.

01:10:30.390 --> 01:10:33.600
The crater had a five-gallon
bucket sitting next to it

01:10:33.600 --> 01:10:35.010
after they had it uncovered,

01:10:35.010 --> 01:10:36.730
and you could extrapolate

01:10:36.730 --> 01:10:37.780
from the size of that bucket

01:10:37.780 --> 01:10:38.770
to the size of the hole

01:10:38.770 --> 01:10:39.883
as to what size the crater was,

01:10:39.883 --> 01:10:42.713
and it was approximately 16 feet across.

01:10:43.830 --> 01:10:45.297
- August 24, 1970.

01:10:45.297 --> 01:10:46.800
It was a Monday morning.

01:10:46.800 --> 01:10:48.960
Karleton Armstrong, his brother Dwight

01:10:48.960 --> 01:10:51.030
and two other perpetrators, Leo Burt

01:10:51.030 --> 01:10:52.560
and one other individual

01:10:52.560 --> 01:10:56.277
drove up to the side of the sterling hall,

01:10:56.277 --> 01:10:57.880
it was a math research building.

01:10:57.880 --> 01:10:59.540
Dow chemical had their offices there.

01:10:59.540 --> 01:11:02.174
It was federal government
as well as the university

01:11:02.174 --> 01:11:04.230
faculty that worked there.

01:11:04.230 --> 01:11:08.310
And they had drove a Ford econoline Van

01:11:08.310 --> 01:11:10.140
stolen from a math professor

01:11:10.140 --> 01:11:13.040
laden with four metal drums,

01:11:13.040 --> 01:11:15.610
50-gallon drums full of
ammonium nitrate and fuel oil.

01:11:15.610 --> 01:11:17.160
The sterling
hall bombing consisted

01:11:17.160 --> 01:11:19.000
of 2,000 pounds of anfo,

01:11:19.000 --> 01:11:21.360
and it was set off right
next to the building.

01:11:21.360 --> 01:11:24.120
The windows were blown in,
the facade was damaged,

01:11:24.120 --> 01:11:26.130
but there was no structural damage.

01:11:26.130 --> 01:11:29.940
In fact, the army math lab
was closed for only one day.

01:11:29.940 --> 01:11:32.370
In Oklahoma city, a similar anfo bomb

01:11:32.370 --> 01:11:36.100
detonated 15 feet away from
a much more robust structure

01:11:36.100 --> 01:11:38.293
and inflicted massive structural damage.

01:11:39.450 --> 01:11:42.350
- What that case did was it
set a, it was a bellwether.

01:11:42.350 --> 01:11:44.220
It set a standard for
us to look at that says,

01:11:44.220 --> 01:11:47.140
okay, if anfo was in fact
used in Oklahoma city,

01:11:47.140 --> 01:11:48.440
why did it not have the characteristics

01:11:48.440 --> 01:11:50.420
that, what occurred in Madison?

01:11:50.420 --> 01:11:53.210
Furthermore, the
signature of an anfo explosion

01:11:53.210 --> 01:11:56.410
is nitric oxide, a noxious gas.

01:11:56.410 --> 01:11:58.080
- There was certainly no fertilizer bomb.

01:11:58.080 --> 01:12:01.240
We know that because there
was no ammonia gas in the air.

01:12:01.240 --> 01:12:04.170
In every other explosion, and they,

01:12:04.170 --> 01:12:05.840
and some students blew up,

01:12:05.840 --> 01:12:07.690
did make an ammonium nitrate bomb,

01:12:07.690 --> 01:12:09.440
but everybody who rushed to that building

01:12:09.440 --> 01:12:10.273
after that explosion

01:12:10.273 --> 01:12:12.080
had to be hospitalized.

01:12:12.080 --> 01:12:14.443
If you ever smelled ammonia strongly,

01:12:15.600 --> 01:12:17.160
and you're talkin' about
goin' into a horse trailer

01:12:17.160 --> 01:12:18.410
or something like it, that's not strong,

01:12:18.410 --> 01:12:19.410
but that'll gag you.

01:12:20.330 --> 01:12:21.420
It will sear your lungs.

01:12:21.420 --> 01:12:24.114
I mean, everybody that
smelled that ammonia gas

01:12:24.114 --> 01:12:26.790
after that ammonium nitrate
bomb at that university

01:12:26.790 --> 01:12:28.830
had to be hospitalized.

01:12:28.830 --> 01:12:30.450
It would have been 30 minutes or an hour,

01:12:30.450 --> 01:12:31.910
depending on how hard
the wind was blowin',

01:12:31.910 --> 01:12:33.810
before anybody could have even approached

01:12:33.810 --> 01:12:35.640
the murrah building if there

01:12:35.640 --> 01:12:38.030
had been an ammonium nitrate bomb.

01:12:38.030 --> 01:12:39.760
- There were other search
and rescue personnel

01:12:39.760 --> 01:12:40.920
that were down there immediately

01:12:40.920 --> 01:12:43.230
from St. Anthony's hospital nearby,

01:12:43.230 --> 01:12:47.473
as well as office employees
from the surrounding offices.

01:12:47.473 --> 01:12:50.140
They would have approached the crime scene

01:12:50.140 --> 01:12:51.690
and buckled over almost immediately,

01:12:51.690 --> 01:12:54.760
vomiting violently, if there
was ammonium nitrate gas.

01:12:54.760 --> 01:12:55.593
There wasn't.

01:12:55.593 --> 01:12:58.170
- I was watching general partin,

01:12:58.170 --> 01:13:00.230
the former head of air
force weapons development,

01:13:00.230 --> 01:13:02.953
point out that the building was blown out,

01:13:02.953 --> 01:13:04.810
that it wasn't the signature

01:13:04.810 --> 01:13:07.200
of an ammonium nitrate fertilizer bomb,

01:13:07.200 --> 01:13:08.770
that there had been a cover up.

01:13:08.770 --> 01:13:10.750
The damaged murrah
building drew the attention

01:13:10.750 --> 01:13:13.000
of retired general Benton k. Partin,

01:13:13.000 --> 01:13:16.030
former director of the air
force armaments laboratory.

01:13:16.030 --> 01:13:17.680
General partin spent his career

01:13:17.680 --> 01:13:20.270
conducting bomb damage
analysis with explosives

01:13:20.270 --> 01:13:21.810
for the military.

01:13:21.810 --> 01:13:24.030
General partin came to Oklahoma city,

01:13:24.030 --> 01:13:25.810
examined the available evidence,

01:13:25.810 --> 01:13:27.650
and rendered a conclusion far different

01:13:27.650 --> 01:13:30.550
than the story being pandered
by the government and media.

01:13:32.330 --> 01:13:35.690
- I spent over 30 years in the air force.

01:13:35.690 --> 01:13:37.540
Most of that was in
research and development.

01:13:37.540 --> 01:13:39.720
I went to a two-year graduate program,

01:13:39.720 --> 01:13:42.000
eight quarters of armament
engineering graduates.

01:13:42.000 --> 01:13:43.677
It was the first course
that was ever set up.

01:13:43.677 --> 01:13:44.510
And after that,

01:13:44.510 --> 01:13:46.650
I worked at the ballistic
research laboratories

01:13:46.650 --> 01:13:49.810
at aberdeen, which was
two years of hands-on work

01:13:49.810 --> 01:13:52.550
designing, developing
containers for rod warheads,

01:13:52.550 --> 01:13:56.010
for the bomarc vessel and
other weapons systems.

01:13:56.010 --> 01:14:00.780
Well, the truck bomb, even
though it was fairly massive,

01:14:00.780 --> 01:14:03.880
was somewhat removed from
some of the structures

01:14:03.880 --> 01:14:05.160
that were damaged.

01:14:05.160 --> 01:14:06.070
It clearly had some,

01:14:06.070 --> 01:14:08.320
what you call brisance damage,

01:14:08.320 --> 01:14:11.100
where the blast pressure was way above

01:14:11.100 --> 01:14:12.090
what you would expect to get

01:14:12.090 --> 01:14:13.739
from the truck at that distance.

01:14:13.739 --> 01:14:16.350
Brisance damage
is that caused by an explosive

01:14:16.350 --> 01:14:18.030
whose blast wave is powerful enough

01:14:18.030 --> 01:14:20.620
to shatter and destroy
the material affected.

01:14:20.620 --> 01:14:23.080
The problem with the failed
columns at the murrah building

01:14:23.080 --> 01:14:26.150
is at that distance, the
air blast from an anfo bomb

01:14:26.150 --> 01:14:28.180
would have been ten times less powerful

01:14:28.180 --> 01:14:29.990
than what was needed to
dissolve the concrete

01:14:29.990 --> 01:14:31.330
and cut the rebar.

01:14:31.330 --> 01:14:34.090
Those columns, had they
failed due to air blast,

01:14:34.090 --> 01:14:36.260
should have broken with
sharp chunks of concrete

01:14:36.260 --> 01:14:37.430
connected by rebar,

01:14:37.430 --> 01:14:40.120
not sheared off at critical points.

01:14:40.120 --> 01:14:42.800
Brisance damage indicates
contact explosives

01:14:42.800 --> 01:14:44.593
placed directly on the beams.

01:14:49.430 --> 01:14:51.480
Even more perplexing is the total collapse

01:14:51.480 --> 01:14:52.630
of column b3,

01:14:52.630 --> 01:14:54.360
which caused the floors on the east side

01:14:54.360 --> 01:14:56.290
to pancake onto one another.

01:14:56.290 --> 01:14:58.867
The building was gutted to
within feet of the other side.

01:14:58.867 --> 01:15:01.220
Column b4, closer to the truck bomb,

01:15:01.220 --> 01:15:02.830
is completely intact.

01:15:02.830 --> 01:15:04.950
Yet we are supposed to
believe that a blast wave

01:15:04.950 --> 01:15:06.490
traveled through b4,

01:15:06.490 --> 01:15:08.490
leaving the sheetrock almost untouched,

01:15:08.490 --> 01:15:11.450
and completely destroyed
the column farther away.

01:15:11.450 --> 01:15:13.330
And most of the front
columns were destroyed

01:15:13.330 --> 01:15:15.470
when the supporting header beam failed,

01:15:15.470 --> 01:15:16.550
but the cause of failure,

01:15:16.550 --> 01:15:18.380
supposedly being air blast,

01:15:18.380 --> 01:15:20.056
should have thrown it into the building.

01:15:20.056 --> 01:15:22.730
Instead, it fell straight down and rolled

01:15:22.730 --> 01:15:24.480
towards the crater.

01:15:24.480 --> 01:15:26.930
General partin's report was conclusive:

01:15:26.930 --> 01:15:28.940
The murrah federal
building was not destroyed

01:15:28.940 --> 01:15:30.553
by one sole truck bomb.

01:15:30.553 --> 01:15:32.460
A major factor in its destruction

01:15:32.460 --> 01:15:34.770
appears to have been
detonation of explosives

01:15:34.770 --> 01:15:37.300
carefully placed at
four critical junctures

01:15:37.300 --> 01:15:39.400
on supporting columns within the building.

01:15:43.090 --> 01:15:44.880
Many independent experts concurred

01:15:44.880 --> 01:15:46.060
with the partin report.

01:15:46.060 --> 01:15:48.320
Sam Cohen, inventor of the neutron bomb,

01:15:48.320 --> 01:15:49.947
issued this statement,

01:15:49.947 --> 01:15:52.330
"I believe that the demolitions
charges in the building,

01:15:52.330 --> 01:15:55.570
that were placed inside at
certain key concrete columns,

01:15:55.570 --> 01:15:58.510
did the primary damage to
the murrah federal building.

01:15:58.510 --> 01:16:00.630
It would have been absolutely impossible,

01:16:00.630 --> 01:16:02.270
and against the laws of nature,

01:16:02.270 --> 01:16:04.370
for a truck full of fertilizer and oil

01:16:04.370 --> 01:16:06.000
no matter how much was used

01:16:06.000 --> 01:16:07.967
to bring the building down."

01:16:08.910 --> 01:16:11.660
The FBI put all their weight
behind the lone bomber theory

01:16:11.660 --> 01:16:14.220
and tailored the evidence
to fit that scenario.

01:16:14.220 --> 01:16:15.490
Dr. Frederic whitehurst,

01:16:15.490 --> 01:16:17.780
a supervisor at the FBI crime lab,

01:16:17.780 --> 01:16:19.910
turned whistleblower over
the bureau's handling

01:16:19.910 --> 01:16:22.520
of the evidence in the
Oklahoma city bombing.

01:16:22.520 --> 01:16:26.110
- Release a report today
condemning the FBI crime lab

01:16:26.110 --> 01:16:29.710
for mishandling evidence and
for slanting its analysis.

01:16:29.710 --> 01:16:32.210
The report is expected
to specifically criticize

01:16:32.210 --> 01:16:34.210
the lab's handling of the Oklahoma city

01:16:34.210 --> 01:16:36.700
and world trade center bombing cases.

01:16:36.700 --> 01:16:39.010
It was the allegations
of FBI whistleblower

01:16:39.010 --> 01:16:42.390
Frederic whitehurst that
sparked that investigation.

01:16:42.390 --> 01:16:44.980
Forced the resign,
Dr. Whitehurst testified

01:16:44.980 --> 01:16:46.440
in Terry Nichols' trial

01:16:46.440 --> 01:16:48.150
that a fellow FBI chemist

01:16:48.150 --> 01:16:50.530
had changed his findings
and lied under oath

01:16:50.530 --> 01:16:52.483
after meeting with federal prosecutors.

01:16:53.550 --> 01:16:56.600
The office of the
inspector general, or oig,

01:16:56.600 --> 01:16:58.530
investigated whitehurst's charges

01:16:58.530 --> 01:17:00.150
and issued a report which concluded

01:17:00.150 --> 01:17:02.980
that the FBI crime lab
had improperly identified

01:17:02.980 --> 01:17:04.800
the characteristics of anfo,

01:17:04.800 --> 01:17:05.910
the weight of the bomb,

01:17:05.910 --> 01:17:07.270
the detonation system,

01:17:07.270 --> 01:17:09.227
and even what kind of explosive was used.

01:17:09.227 --> 01:17:11.500
- The Oklahoma city case
will get a lot of attention

01:17:11.500 --> 01:17:13.410
because what the inspector general goes on

01:17:13.410 --> 01:17:15.710
at some length to say in his analysis

01:17:15.710 --> 01:17:19.610
of an agent testimony in
some of the pre-trial stages

01:17:19.610 --> 01:17:21.270
is that one agent in particular

01:17:21.270 --> 01:17:24.270
made sort of seat-of-the-pants estimates

01:17:24.270 --> 01:17:25.650
about the Oklahoma city bomb,

01:17:25.650 --> 01:17:27.440
but then couched them in his reports,

01:17:27.440 --> 01:17:28.730
in his written reports,

01:17:28.730 --> 01:17:30.860
as being the result of
scientific evidence.

01:17:30.860 --> 01:17:33.950
- The FBI laboratory's billed
itself for many, many years

01:17:33.950 --> 01:17:36.660
as the premier forensic
laboratory in the world.

01:17:36.660 --> 01:17:38.350
The people that did the things they did

01:17:38.350 --> 01:17:40.300
knew doggone well what they were doing.

01:17:44.240 --> 01:17:45.640
The Wright
armament laboratory

01:17:45.640 --> 01:17:46.700
at eglin air force base

01:17:46.700 --> 01:17:48.610
conducted a series of explosive tests

01:17:48.610 --> 01:17:51.660
to compare their data to
the bombing in Oklahoma.

01:17:51.660 --> 01:17:53.963
The eglin test structure
was a simple, three-story

01:17:53.963 --> 01:17:57.150
concrete slab building
with no support columns.

01:17:57.150 --> 01:18:00.120
The engineers at eglin tried
to recreate the truck bomb

01:18:00.120 --> 01:18:03.020
as McVeigh and the FBI
claimed it was constructed,

01:18:03.020 --> 01:18:06.690
with 4,000 pounds of anfo
packed into a dozen barrels.

01:18:06.690 --> 01:18:09.800
But they found that each barrel
acted as a separate bomb,

01:18:09.800 --> 01:18:11.984
canceling out the explosive
force of each other

01:18:11.984 --> 01:18:14.510
and pushing most of the blast upwards.

01:18:14.510 --> 01:18:17.320
So they constructed a
single, more powerful bomb

01:18:17.320 --> 01:18:19.920
and exploded it outside
the target building

01:18:19.920 --> 01:18:22.060
to test the effects of air blast.

01:18:22.060 --> 01:18:24.080
They found that their
weaker test structure

01:18:24.080 --> 01:18:26.603
suffered less damage
from a more powerful bomb

01:18:26.603 --> 01:18:29.193
than was supposedly used at Oklahoma city.

01:18:31.430 --> 01:18:33.200
The report for the Wright laboratory

01:18:33.200 --> 01:18:35.517
at eglin air force base concluded

01:18:35.517 --> 01:18:37.760
"the damage at the murrah federal building

01:18:37.760 --> 01:18:40.370
is not the result of
the truck bomb itself,

01:18:40.370 --> 01:18:42.180
but rather due to other factors such

01:18:42.180 --> 01:18:44.910
as locally placed charges
within the building."

01:18:44.910 --> 01:18:46.410
The evidence is undeniable,

01:18:46.410 --> 01:18:48.720
despite the pleas of the official story,

01:18:48.720 --> 01:18:50.970
that the Ryder truck bomb
was not the sole cause

01:18:50.970 --> 01:18:52.350
of destruction that day,

01:18:52.350 --> 01:18:54.490
that there were bombs
placed inside the building

01:18:54.490 --> 01:18:56.150
which caused the brunt of casualties

01:18:56.150 --> 01:18:58.223
as floors collapsed on helpless victims.

01:19:05.345 --> 01:19:08.120
- And the rescuers apparently
had to abandon the people

01:19:08.120 --> 01:19:10.260
they were trying to rescue temporarily.

01:19:10.260 --> 01:19:11.093
Now were you there

01:19:11.093 --> 01:19:12.550
a minute ago when somebody yelled,

01:19:12.550 --> 01:19:13.990
they thought they'd seen a second device?

01:19:13.990 --> 01:19:15.215
- Yes, sir, we were in the,

01:19:15.215 --> 01:19:18.980
close to the parkin' area
trying to recover a victim.

01:19:18.980 --> 01:19:20.580
As rescuers desperately tried

01:19:20.580 --> 01:19:22.420
to free the victims from the rubble,

01:19:22.420 --> 01:19:24.330
several evacuations of the site,

01:19:24.330 --> 01:19:26.980
due to reports of other
bombs, impeded these efforts.

01:19:27.970 --> 01:19:29.580
- At some point, we got to the corner

01:19:29.580 --> 01:19:31.460
of fifth and I believe it was Robinson,

01:19:31.460 --> 01:19:32.970
right there are the corner
of the murrah building,

01:19:32.970 --> 01:19:35.230
and we heard "second bomb."

01:19:35.230 --> 01:19:36.560
Somebody yelled "second bomb."

01:19:36.560 --> 01:19:39.048
I stopped, I turned around,

01:19:39.048 --> 01:19:40.913
people were runnin' past me,

01:19:41.776 --> 01:19:45.000
and I just kind of watched
what, what was unfolding.

01:19:45.000 --> 01:19:47.050
Of course, never, nothing ever did happen.

01:19:47.050 --> 01:19:48.900
The Oklahoma
highway patrol reported

01:19:48.900 --> 01:19:51.310
that another explosive device was found.

01:19:51.310 --> 01:19:53.760
The Oklahoma city fire
department confirmed that.

01:19:54.620 --> 01:19:56.220
Defense department logs recorded

01:19:56.220 --> 01:19:58.410
that a second bomb was disarmed,

01:19:58.410 --> 01:19:59.993
a third bomb was evacuated.

01:20:00.978 --> 01:20:05.140
- The explosive that
they disarmed last night

01:20:05.140 --> 01:20:06.740
was even larger.

01:20:06.740 --> 01:20:08.670
Who planted
these bombs and had access

01:20:08.670 --> 01:20:11.030
to the murrah building before the bombing?

01:20:11.030 --> 01:20:13.000
A deputy sheriff recorded this footage

01:20:13.000 --> 01:20:15.180
during one of the evacuations.

01:20:15.180 --> 01:20:18.270
Here, the atf is seen
pulling out several weapons

01:20:18.270 --> 01:20:21.205
and blocks of what appear
to be plastic explosive.

01:20:21.205 --> 01:20:23.640
Was this the source of the bomb scare,

01:20:23.640 --> 01:20:26.330
or did this ordnance come
from an illegal armory

01:20:26.330 --> 01:20:29.544
that witnesses report the atf
kept in the murrah building?

01:20:29.544 --> 01:20:32.300
The atf denies they kept
any weapons or explosives

01:20:32.300 --> 01:20:33.133
in the building.

01:20:35.880 --> 01:20:39.080
- Day one, hour two of the bombing,

01:20:39.080 --> 01:20:40.630
the most significant event that happened

01:20:40.630 --> 01:20:42.990
is when they said they found
other bombs in the building.

01:20:42.990 --> 01:20:44.770
The second most significant
event was the way

01:20:44.770 --> 01:20:47.500
they moved everybody
back and held 'em back.

01:20:47.500 --> 01:20:49.815
There were still people alive
trapped in the building,

01:20:49.815 --> 01:20:51.680
but they came in with two trucks

01:20:51.680 --> 01:20:53.190
and backed them up to the murrah building

01:20:53.190 --> 01:20:54.740
and a bunch of these guys

01:20:54.740 --> 01:20:57.360
dressed in blue jackets
with no letters on the back

01:20:57.360 --> 01:20:59.010
started taking boxes of files out

01:20:59.010 --> 01:21:00.610
and puttin' 'em on this truck.

01:21:00.610 --> 01:21:05.270
- We were told by a blonde female agent

01:21:05.270 --> 01:21:06.500
that there were files

01:21:07.540 --> 01:21:10.930
so serious to the government

01:21:10.930 --> 01:21:12.680
that until those files were relocated,

01:21:12.680 --> 01:21:14.810
there would not be any recovery effort.

01:21:14.810 --> 01:21:18.257
- If you remember the whitewater
investigation in Arkansas,

01:21:18.257 --> 01:21:20.680
all the paperwork was stored
in the murrah building.

01:21:20.680 --> 01:21:23.620
They had FBI agents over in the fields

01:21:23.620 --> 01:21:26.860
to the west of the murrah
building pickin' up paper

01:21:26.860 --> 01:21:28.820
almost all day long.

01:21:28.820 --> 01:21:31.090
- And it was during this time that,

01:21:31.090 --> 01:21:32.170
early in the investigation,

01:21:32.170 --> 01:21:33.400
that I started receiving

01:21:33.400 --> 01:21:35.350
some various phone calls.

01:21:35.350 --> 01:21:38.670
One of them was a phone call
from little rock, Arkansas.

01:21:38.670 --> 01:21:40.500
The guy said that he was a federal agent,

01:21:40.500 --> 01:21:43.670
he was not an FBI agent, he was not atf,

01:21:43.670 --> 01:21:46.410
but what he did say was
during their investigation

01:21:46.410 --> 01:21:49.300
of the Clintons on all the drug running

01:21:49.300 --> 01:21:50.760
that went through mena, Arkansas,

01:21:50.760 --> 01:21:52.550
and, you know, lasater's ranch

01:21:52.550 --> 01:21:54.640
and all of that stuff that
was going on at the time

01:21:54.640 --> 01:21:56.210
during Iran-contra,

01:21:56.210 --> 01:22:00.640
that those records, when
Clinton went to Washington,

01:22:00.640 --> 01:22:02.810
were transferred from there
to the murrah building.

01:22:02.810 --> 01:22:04.390
- Because of the additional bomb threats

01:22:04.390 --> 01:22:05.930
or because the building was unstable

01:22:05.930 --> 01:22:08.166
and the firefighters couldn't get to them,

01:22:08.166 --> 01:22:09.823
so those are, a lot of
patients, I think, were lost

01:22:09.823 --> 01:22:11.570
that could have been saved.

01:22:11.570 --> 01:22:13.680
After rescue
and recovery had been halted,

01:22:13.680 --> 01:22:15.360
the building was prepped for demolition

01:22:15.360 --> 01:22:17.460
even though all the bodies
had not been recovered,

01:22:17.460 --> 01:22:20.790
and despite the architect's
report that it could be rebuilt.

01:22:20.790 --> 01:22:22.030
The investigative team from

01:22:22.030 --> 01:22:23.950
the American society of civil engineers

01:22:23.950 --> 01:22:25.770
was not allowed on site.

01:22:25.770 --> 01:22:27.130
The defense lawyers for McVeigh

01:22:27.130 --> 01:22:29.610
were able to visit the site one time,

01:22:29.610 --> 01:22:31.220
but even then, they were not allowed

01:22:31.220 --> 01:22:32.170
to view the crater.

01:22:35.760 --> 01:22:38.050
- They were going to halt
it on the 29th of April,

01:22:38.050 --> 01:22:39.270
they were gonna halt the recovery

01:22:39.270 --> 01:22:41.620
and prepare the building to be imploded.

01:22:41.620 --> 01:22:43.840
We went back in after the final demolition

01:22:43.840 --> 01:22:46.420
to relocate two victims

01:22:46.420 --> 01:22:47.280
that we knew that we had left

01:22:47.280 --> 01:22:49.420
and a possibility of a third victim,

01:22:49.420 --> 01:22:50.870
which we also located him.

01:22:50.870 --> 01:22:53.390
I don't know why they were in such a rush.

01:22:53.390 --> 01:22:55.620
Gsa was saying the building was unsafe

01:22:55.620 --> 01:22:57.370
and needed to be brought down.

01:22:57.370 --> 01:22:58.590
A month after the bombing,

01:22:58.590 --> 01:23:00.180
the Alfred p. Murrah federal building

01:23:00.180 --> 01:23:02.740
was completely demolished
with less than 200 pounds

01:23:02.740 --> 01:23:04.010
of explosives.

01:23:04.010 --> 01:23:06.380
The wreckage was buried under armed guard,

01:23:06.380 --> 01:23:08.550
and one can only think
that certain officials

01:23:08.550 --> 01:23:11.430
breathed a sigh of relief as
the outstanding counterpoint

01:23:11.430 --> 01:23:14.623
to the official story
disappeared in a cloud of dust.

01:23:23.490 --> 01:23:25.760
Tidbits of truth about
the Oklahoma city bombing

01:23:25.760 --> 01:23:28.890
would often come from the
most unlikely of places.

01:23:28.890 --> 01:23:30.580
Another strange and brutal murder,

01:23:30.580 --> 01:23:32.900
at first seemingly
unrelated to the bombing,

01:23:32.900 --> 01:23:35.450
would set the stage for some
of the most damning evidence

01:23:35.450 --> 01:23:38.440
that the government was
withholding from the public.

01:23:38.440 --> 01:23:40.450
- My name is Jesse trentadue.

01:23:40.450 --> 01:23:42.600
I'm an attorney from salt lake city, Utah.

01:23:42.600 --> 01:23:44.150
My brother Kenneth Michael trentadue

01:23:44.150 --> 01:23:46.630
was murdered in the
federal transfer center

01:23:46.630 --> 01:23:50.810
here in Oklahoma city in August of 1995.

01:23:50.810 --> 01:23:52.420
Kenny had a hard life.

01:23:52.420 --> 01:23:54.280
You know, I often thought about that,

01:23:54.280 --> 01:23:58.180
and how he ended up the way he did.

01:23:58.180 --> 01:24:03.020
He was an incredibly bright
man, an incredible athlete.

01:24:03.020 --> 01:24:05.120
He set the national record in high school

01:24:05.120 --> 01:24:06.870
for the two-mile run as a freshman.

01:24:08.550 --> 01:24:11.910
Went into the service,
and like so many boys did

01:24:11.910 --> 01:24:14.560
during the Vietnam war, they
come out heroin addicts.

01:24:16.000 --> 01:24:19.625
He robbed banks, two banks
to support that habit.

01:24:19.625 --> 01:24:21.340
He was caught and he pled guilty.

01:24:21.340 --> 01:24:22.300
He went and did his time.

01:24:22.300 --> 01:24:24.703
He was a very strong guy.

01:24:25.550 --> 01:24:27.730
He wasn't very big but he was very tough.

01:24:27.730 --> 01:24:29.790
He was easygoing,

01:24:29.790 --> 01:24:30.890
but he wouldn't back down.

01:24:30.890 --> 01:24:32.710
So if you pushed him,

01:24:32.710 --> 01:24:34.070
you were gonna get a fight,

01:24:34.070 --> 01:24:36.160
and it was a fight you were gonna lose.

01:24:36.160 --> 01:24:38.225
We loved him and stood behind him,

01:24:38.225 --> 01:24:39.600
and he was a good man.

01:24:39.600 --> 01:24:41.070
Kenny was supposedly arrested

01:24:41.070 --> 01:24:43.070
for a probation violation

01:24:43.070 --> 01:24:46.505
and sent to Oklahoma city
at the transfer center

01:24:46.505 --> 01:24:48.830
for a probation hearing.

01:24:48.830 --> 01:24:51.813
We now know that that's crap.

01:24:53.080 --> 01:24:55.720
I said to him, "Kenny, what,
what are you doing there?"

01:24:55.720 --> 01:24:56.880
And he says, "well, they sent me back here

01:24:56.880 --> 01:24:58.197
for a probation hearing."

01:24:58.197 --> 01:25:00.254
And we talked about getting him a lawyer,

01:25:00.254 --> 01:25:03.930
and the fact that we didn't
expect him to do more

01:25:03.930 --> 01:25:06.120
than a couple months.

01:25:06.120 --> 01:25:08.020
And so my mother called me at work,

01:25:08.020 --> 01:25:09.780
it was about seven in the morning,

01:25:09.780 --> 01:25:12.023
and told me that, and
I couldn't believe it,

01:25:13.539 --> 01:25:14.890
and that Kenny had
supposedly killed himself,

01:25:14.890 --> 01:25:17.333
'cause I had just spoken
with him the night before.

01:25:18.230 --> 01:25:20.360
There's no way in hell he
would have killed himself.

01:25:20.360 --> 01:25:22.980
This is not a guy who kills himself.

01:25:22.980 --> 01:25:26.750
I mean, his life is the
best it's ever been.

01:25:26.750 --> 01:25:29.593
I found out later that an
autopsy had already been done.

01:25:30.500 --> 01:25:32.040
Now, the government,
the federal government

01:25:32.040 --> 01:25:33.113
didn't want one done,

01:25:34.000 --> 01:25:35.760
but the state of Oklahoma required one

01:25:35.760 --> 01:25:37.383
for a death in incarceration.

01:25:38.240 --> 01:25:40.510
So the federal government didn't know

01:25:40.510 --> 01:25:41.387
that there was an autopsy done,

01:25:41.387 --> 01:25:43.704
and did not want the autopsy done,

01:25:43.704 --> 01:25:46.700
and the federal government went twice

01:25:46.700 --> 01:25:48.550
to the medical examiner's office

01:25:48.550 --> 01:25:50.183
asking to have Kenny cremated.

01:25:51.470 --> 01:25:54.313
It took a week to get his
body released and home,

01:25:55.600 --> 01:25:57.130
and I kept getting the run around

01:25:57.130 --> 01:25:58.470
from the federal
government, and then finally

01:25:58.470 --> 01:25:59.617
I just screamed in the phone one day,

01:25:59.617 --> 01:26:01.640
"why don't you keep him?"

01:26:01.640 --> 01:26:02.970
And when the body comes home,

01:26:02.970 --> 01:26:04.140
it's totally made up

01:26:04.140 --> 01:26:06.400
so you can't see the wounds.

01:26:06.400 --> 01:26:09.063
He was beaten head to toe,

01:26:10.090 --> 01:26:12.140
his skull was smashed in in three places.

01:26:13.080 --> 01:26:16.830
The soles of his feet had been beaten.

01:26:16.830 --> 01:26:20.850
You could see the fingerprint
bruises on his arm

01:26:20.850 --> 01:26:21.900
where he'd been held.

01:26:23.210 --> 01:26:24.160
His throat was cut

01:26:25.440 --> 01:26:26.640
and he'd been strangled.

01:26:27.730 --> 01:26:31.430
And the federal government said
it was a suicide by hanging.

01:26:31.430 --> 01:26:33.600
When his body's turned over
to the medical examiner

01:26:33.600 --> 01:26:36.980
two hours later, he's wearing
nothing but boxer shorts.

01:26:36.980 --> 01:26:38.660
The government said they
don't know what happened

01:26:38.660 --> 01:26:39.493
to the clothes.

01:26:41.419 --> 01:26:44.550
They cleaned the cell that morning

01:26:44.550 --> 01:26:47.680
so the medical examiner can't
do an examination of it,

01:26:47.680 --> 01:26:51.330
and the medical examiner's
not allowed into the cell

01:26:51.330 --> 01:26:52.413
for six months.

01:26:53.920 --> 01:26:55.550
And when he finally is allowed in,

01:26:55.550 --> 01:26:57.820
he does a test that's called luminol

01:26:57.820 --> 01:27:00.380
that will reveal the presence of blood.

01:27:00.380 --> 01:27:02.743
And Fred Jordan told
me that the cell lit up

01:27:02.743 --> 01:27:03.913
like a Christmas tree.

01:27:04.850 --> 01:27:08.200
The logbooks involving
my brother disappeared.

01:27:08.200 --> 01:27:09.780
The ones that didn't disappear,

01:27:09.780 --> 01:27:11.883
the pages from the logbooks are missing.

01:27:13.410 --> 01:27:15.323
The crime scene photographs disappear.

01:27:16.400 --> 01:27:19.150
The negatives of the crime
scene photographs disappear.

01:27:20.923 --> 01:27:25.530
The video camera supposedly malfunctions.

01:27:25.530 --> 01:27:28.480
Within an hour of death,
he'd consumed the equivalent

01:27:28.480 --> 01:27:30.750
of 30 bottles of Coca-Cola,

01:27:30.750 --> 01:27:34.060
and Dr. Jordan told me
that caffeine is used

01:27:34.060 --> 01:27:37.120
in a lot of countries,
like third world countries,

01:27:37.120 --> 01:27:39.440
to enhance pain under torture.

01:27:39.440 --> 01:27:40.970
And he also told me that the beatings

01:27:40.970 --> 01:27:45.223
on the soles of the feet
were indicative of torture.

01:27:46.110 --> 01:27:48.100
And I believe it was the FBI.

01:27:48.100 --> 01:27:50.770
I firmly believe that
for a lot of reasons now.

01:27:50.770 --> 01:27:52.490
I didn't start out believing that.

01:27:52.490 --> 01:27:54.474
I started out trusting them

01:27:54.474 --> 01:27:57.240
until I could see what they were doing.

01:27:57.240 --> 01:27:59.978
And they would come to
me asking for information

01:27:59.978 --> 01:28:04.902
and then immediately go
and destroy the evidence,

01:28:04.902 --> 01:28:06.433
threaten the witness,

01:28:07.570 --> 01:28:10.708
do everything they could
to prevent the case

01:28:10.708 --> 01:28:12.313
from being made a murder.

01:28:13.360 --> 01:28:14.460
People were leaking me stuff.

01:28:14.460 --> 01:28:16.952
They wanted me to know, they wouldn't,

01:28:16.952 --> 01:28:17.785
didn't want me to know who they were.

01:28:17.785 --> 01:28:21.120
Late December of '95, early January of '96

01:28:21.120 --> 01:28:22.070
I get a phone call.

01:28:23.500 --> 01:28:25.530
The person won't leave their name.

01:28:25.530 --> 01:28:28.460
The person said, "your brother
was killed by the FBI."

01:28:28.460 --> 01:28:31.360
They said, "it was an
interrogation that went bad."

01:28:31.360 --> 01:28:33.790
It was a case of mistaken identity,

01:28:33.790 --> 01:28:38.070
that he fit a profile of
people who were robbing banks

01:28:38.070 --> 01:28:40.423
to get money to attack
the federal government.

01:28:41.640 --> 01:28:43.150
Just before he was executed,

01:28:43.150 --> 01:28:45.163
I get a message from Tim McVeigh,

01:28:46.170 --> 01:28:47.127
and he told me, he said,

01:28:47.127 --> 01:28:48.850
"when I saw your brother's picture

01:28:50.090 --> 01:28:51.470
and heard what happened to him,

01:28:51.470 --> 01:28:55.050
I wanted you to know that
I think the FBI killed him

01:28:55.050 --> 01:28:57.780
because they thought he
was Richard Lee Guthrie."

01:28:57.780 --> 01:28:58.910
Early on, the FBI

01:28:58.910 --> 01:29:00.520
had investigated the possibility

01:29:00.520 --> 01:29:02.160
that a string of bank robberies committed

01:29:02.160 --> 01:29:05.000
by what the media dubbed
"the midwest bank robbers"

01:29:05.000 --> 01:29:06.830
had financed the bombing.

01:29:06.830 --> 01:29:08.710
Led by Peter langan and
Richard Lee Guthrie,

01:29:08.710 --> 01:29:11.300
aka "wild bill," the
gang called themselves

01:29:11.300 --> 01:29:13.280
the Aryan republican army.

01:29:13.280 --> 01:29:14.520
The purpose of the robberies?

01:29:14.520 --> 01:29:15.530
To finance a race war

01:29:15.530 --> 01:29:17.350
within the United States.

01:29:17.350 --> 01:29:19.040
Wild bill closely resembled

01:29:19.040 --> 01:29:20.980
some of the John Doe number two sketches

01:29:20.980 --> 01:29:23.730
and had a tattoo similar to
that reported by witnesses.

01:29:24.740 --> 01:29:27.020
In an affidavit, Peter langan revealed

01:29:27.020 --> 01:29:29.820
that a member of the ara
had admitted to liabilities

01:29:29.820 --> 01:29:31.320
concerning the bombing.

01:29:31.320 --> 01:29:32.847
Another member had threatened,

01:29:32.847 --> 01:29:34.230
"we're going to get them.

01:29:34.230 --> 01:29:35.470
We're gonna hit one of their buildings

01:29:35.470 --> 01:29:36.550
during the middle of the day.

01:29:36.550 --> 01:29:39.090
It's going to be a federal building."

01:29:39.090 --> 01:29:41.490
Most of the ara was
arrested for bank robberies

01:29:41.490 --> 01:29:42.910
soon after the bombing.

01:29:42.910 --> 01:29:44.790
Peter langan offered
to provide information

01:29:44.790 --> 01:29:47.700
about his co-conspirators'
relationship with McVeigh.

01:29:47.700 --> 01:29:49.533
This offer was refused.

01:29:50.650 --> 01:29:51.850
- Then I got a call from

01:29:54.049 --> 01:29:56.453
a great guy, j.D. Cash.

01:29:57.390 --> 01:30:00.645
He was a hunting and fishing reporter

01:30:00.645 --> 01:30:04.893
at the mccurtain county
news in eastern Oklahoma.

01:30:06.010 --> 01:30:08.120
He had friends that were
killed in the bombing,

01:30:08.120 --> 01:30:09.593
and family, wounded.

01:30:10.940 --> 01:30:12.140
And one day, he calls me up

01:30:12.140 --> 01:30:13.807
and he says, "Jesse, can I talk to you?"

01:30:13.807 --> 01:30:15.050
And I said, "well, sure, who are you?"

01:30:15.050 --> 01:30:17.377
He says, "I'm j.D. Cash," and he says,

01:30:17.377 --> 01:30:18.767
"I'm investigating the
bombing in Oklahoma."

01:30:18.767 --> 01:30:21.960
And he said, "I'm interested
in your brother's death.

01:30:21.960 --> 01:30:24.730
Can I ask you some
questions," and I said, "yes."

01:30:24.730 --> 01:30:27.880
And j.D. Said, "well,
did he have any tattoos?"

01:30:27.880 --> 01:30:29.200
And I said, "yes."

01:30:29.200 --> 01:30:30.330
And he said, "what, and where?"

01:30:30.330 --> 01:30:35.150
I said, "a dragon tattoo
on his left forearm."

01:30:35.150 --> 01:30:36.397
J.d. Said, "oh my god."

01:30:38.560 --> 01:30:40.907
He said, "are you setting
down," I said, "yeah."

01:30:41.970 --> 01:30:42.803
He said, "lemme tell you this."

01:30:42.803 --> 01:30:44.715
He said, "when your brother was picked up

01:30:44.715 --> 01:30:46.030
and sent to Oklahoma,

01:30:46.030 --> 01:30:47.530
the largest manhunt in American history

01:30:47.530 --> 01:30:49.337
was in place for John Doe two."

01:30:50.380 --> 01:30:53.810
We didn't start out to solve
the Oklahoma city bombing case,

01:30:53.810 --> 01:30:56.800
we started out for justice for my brother.

01:30:56.800 --> 01:31:00.983
But every lead, every trail,

01:31:02.700 --> 01:31:04.550
every bit of important evidence,

01:31:04.550 --> 01:31:06.960
has brought us to the
Oklahoma city bombing.

01:31:06.960 --> 01:31:08.280
Now, the freedom of information act

01:31:08.280 --> 01:31:10.430
is an act congress passes,
it says the government

01:31:10.430 --> 01:31:15.117
is supposed to turn over
documents and information to you

01:31:15.117 --> 01:31:19.000
that you request, unless
there's a good reason not to,

01:31:19.000 --> 01:31:20.940
such as national security.

01:31:20.940 --> 01:31:24.248
I bring the first foia suit,
saying I want all documents

01:31:24.248 --> 01:31:29.248
showing a link between the FBI

01:31:30.080 --> 01:31:32.453
and the southern poverty law center,

01:31:33.350 --> 01:31:34.743
and the Oklahoma city bombing.

01:31:36.260 --> 01:31:40.360
And the FBI comes back

01:31:41.780 --> 01:31:43.673
and says there are no documents.

01:31:45.390 --> 01:31:48.340
They didn't know that i'd
been leaked two teletypes

01:31:48.340 --> 01:31:53.030
from FBI director Louis freeh,
then-director Louis freeh,

01:31:53.030 --> 01:31:56.200
talking about elohim city,
talking about informants,

01:31:56.200 --> 01:31:58.320
talking about the southern
poverty law center,

01:31:58.320 --> 01:32:01.870
talking about the fact that
McVeigh had called elohim city

01:32:01.870 --> 01:32:04.370
two days before the bombing,
asking for more help.

01:32:05.250 --> 01:32:06.770
So I sue them, and they walk in the court,

01:32:06.770 --> 01:32:09.060
and they tell the federal
judge there's no documents.

01:32:09.060 --> 01:32:10.373
Well, I filed those, too.

01:32:11.500 --> 01:32:13.627
The federal judge looks at 'em, he says,

01:32:13.627 --> 01:32:16.164
"you go back, and you do a manual search,

01:32:16.164 --> 01:32:18.847
and you bring everything
you find back in the court."

01:32:19.850 --> 01:32:21.580
Well, then they come back
and plead with the judge,

01:32:21.580 --> 01:32:25.310
and they say, "judge,
we promised anonymity,"

01:32:25.310 --> 01:32:27.760
and if we have to
disclose these documents,

01:32:27.760 --> 01:32:29.265
it will reveal their names,

01:32:29.265 --> 01:32:31.230
and their lives will be in jeopardy."

01:32:31.230 --> 01:32:33.580
German citizen
Andreas Carl strassmeir,

01:32:33.580 --> 01:32:36.000
aka Andy the German, came to the U.S.

01:32:36.000 --> 01:32:37.640
In the early '90s.

01:32:37.640 --> 01:32:40.080
Professing Neo-Nazi beliefs,
he moved to elohim city,

01:32:40.080 --> 01:32:42.230
becoming their chief of security.

01:32:42.230 --> 01:32:45.521
He was reported by atf
informant Carol howe and others

01:32:45.521 --> 01:32:47.796
to make threats about
bombing federal buildings

01:32:47.796 --> 01:32:50.850
and assassinations of public officials.

01:32:50.850 --> 01:32:53.289
It is known that McVeigh
called elohim city twice,

01:32:53.289 --> 01:32:55.400
looking for the mysterious German,

01:32:55.400 --> 01:32:58.420
when members of the ara
were living with strassmeir.

01:32:58.420 --> 01:33:00.310
McVeigh also attempted
to reach Andy's attorney,

01:33:00.310 --> 01:33:03.710
kirk lyons, by phone, in
the days before the bombing.

01:33:03.710 --> 01:33:05.400
- We started looking at
strassmeir real hard,

01:33:05.400 --> 01:33:06.930
and this guy didn't add up, either.

01:33:06.930 --> 01:33:09.330
He was on special assignment,
and disappears and shows up

01:33:09.330 --> 01:33:11.720
in elohim city, came in through Texas,

01:33:11.720 --> 01:33:13.780
and was placed at elohim city.

01:33:13.780 --> 01:33:16.390
Now, why elohim city, I
mean, nobody in Germany,

01:33:16.390 --> 01:33:17.407
if I haven't heard of elohim city,

01:33:17.407 --> 01:33:19.590
and I live in Oklahoma,
how's anybody in Germany

01:33:19.590 --> 01:33:20.880
hear of this place?

01:33:20.880 --> 01:33:24.460
Well, evidently, it was from
a lawyer named kirk lyons.

01:33:24.460 --> 01:33:27.010
I start putting dots together.

01:33:27.010 --> 01:33:28.640
I start finding out who these people are

01:33:28.640 --> 01:33:30.110
and who they know, who they run with

01:33:30.110 --> 01:33:32.290
and what their background
and what their history is.

01:33:32.290 --> 01:33:35.181
And we create a picture from this.

01:33:35.181 --> 01:33:39.842
We have strassmeir doing all
this paramilitary training,

01:33:39.842 --> 01:33:42.030
takes over as chief of security of a place

01:33:42.030 --> 01:33:43.930
that didn't need any security.

01:33:43.930 --> 01:33:45.700
Tells 'em they need to
get rid of their shotguns

01:33:45.700 --> 01:33:48.893
and deer rifles and buy
assault rifles and skss,

01:33:48.893 --> 01:33:50.280
and aks, and stuff like this,

01:33:50.280 --> 01:33:52.140
because they're gonna be the next waco.

01:33:52.140 --> 01:33:54.520
Well, he scares 'em down there,
they don't know what to do.

01:33:54.520 --> 01:33:58.060
So they start, you know, gearin' up for

01:33:58.060 --> 01:34:00.640
the last days of the book of revelation.

01:34:00.640 --> 01:34:02.450
- Strassmeir's an interesting character,

01:34:02.450 --> 01:34:04.350
these documents we got from the court.

01:34:05.430 --> 01:34:08.550
It's my understanding he's a
German intelligence officer.

01:34:08.550 --> 01:34:12.413
He's, apparently, after the bombing,

01:34:12.413 --> 01:34:15.690
taken out of the country
by a former CIA operative,

01:34:15.690 --> 01:34:17.360
back to Germany.

01:34:17.360 --> 01:34:19.440
His visa, as I understand had expired,

01:34:19.440 --> 01:34:22.660
and no one picked him up,
and he was smuggled out

01:34:22.660 --> 01:34:24.130
through Mexico, and back to Germany.

01:34:24.130 --> 01:34:29.130
- I said "why wasn't Andy
strassmeir questioned?"

01:34:30.378 --> 01:34:32.783
And one of the attorneys said,
"oh, we did question him."

01:34:32.783 --> 01:34:37.680
I said, 'yeah, but you waited
until he got back to Germany,

01:34:38.880 --> 01:34:42.130
and then you called him up
over the phone and asked him

01:34:42.130 --> 01:34:44.490
did he have anything to
do with the bombing."

01:34:44.490 --> 01:34:49.083
- In Tulsa, at lady godiva's,
which is a strip bar,

01:34:50.363 --> 01:34:52.793
one of the strippers, named Shanti,

01:34:54.130 --> 01:34:57.680
said that McVeigh, and strassmeir,

01:34:57.680 --> 01:34:59.980
and several people had come

01:34:59.980 --> 01:35:03.020
in a few days before the bombing,

01:35:03.020 --> 01:35:05.270
and there was a Ryder truck
parked out in the parking lot.

01:35:05.270 --> 01:35:08.450
- What we can say about
Timothy McVeigh's connections

01:35:08.450 --> 01:35:12.300
to elohim city is that he
called there at least twice,

01:35:12.300 --> 01:35:15.330
once on April 5th and once on April 17th,

01:35:15.330 --> 01:35:18.706
that he checked into a motel
within miles from there,

01:35:18.706 --> 01:35:20.550
that he received a speeding ticket

01:35:20.550 --> 01:35:23.186
within miles from there,
and that he also calls

01:35:23.186 --> 01:35:28.186
outlying areas of elohim city
residents or acquaintances.

01:35:30.500 --> 01:35:35.500
So, very briefly, those are
his provable connections

01:35:35.960 --> 01:35:37.193
to elohim city.

01:35:38.350 --> 01:35:39.450
The southern
poverty law center,

01:35:39.450 --> 01:35:40.620
along with the FBI,

01:35:40.620 --> 01:35:42.850
kept informants in elohim city.

01:35:42.850 --> 01:35:44.187
One of these may have been strassmeir,

01:35:44.187 --> 01:35:46.310
the supposed Neo-Nazi.

01:35:46.310 --> 01:35:47.814
Known primarily for its work in litigating

01:35:47.814 --> 01:35:49.670
against hate groups,

01:35:49.670 --> 01:35:52.300
and its outspoken chief
counsel, Morris dees,

01:35:52.300 --> 01:35:54.270
the splc has also become

01:35:54.270 --> 01:35:57.230
an informal intelligence-gathering
arm of the FBI,

01:35:57.230 --> 01:35:59.650
and now, the department
of homeland security.

01:35:59.650 --> 01:36:01.940
They share the same interest
with the federal government

01:36:01.940 --> 01:36:05.060
in suppressing what they
knew about prior knowledge.

01:36:05.060 --> 01:36:07.847
- By the FBI's own admission,
there were at least

01:36:07.847 --> 01:36:10.453
between four and six
informants at elohim city.

01:36:11.860 --> 01:36:13.670
I don't know what the
population of elohim city is,

01:36:13.670 --> 01:36:16.263
but it sounds like, whenever
three people get together

01:36:16.263 --> 01:36:19.533
to talk about overthrowing the government,

01:36:19.533 --> 01:36:21.180
two of 'em are working for the government.

01:36:21.180 --> 01:36:23.320
Andy strassmeir's
roommate at elohim city

01:36:23.320 --> 01:36:26.440
was Michael Brescia, a young
skinhead from Philadelphia

01:36:26.440 --> 01:36:28.850
who was also a member of the ara.

01:36:28.850 --> 01:36:30.630
He was later convicted for bank robbery,

01:36:30.630 --> 01:36:32.360
and also bore a striking resemblance

01:36:32.360 --> 01:36:34.934
to the John Doe number two sketches.

01:36:34.934 --> 01:36:37.490
The FBI and the atf had something to hide

01:36:37.490 --> 01:36:38.920
in eastern Oklahoma.

01:36:38.920 --> 01:36:40.700
Was McVeigh in elohim city?

01:36:40.700 --> 01:36:42.433
If so, what was he doing?

01:36:44.320 --> 01:36:49.320
- My name's Josiah stone, and
I was on a spiritual journey.

01:36:49.700 --> 01:36:53.500
I integrated quite
quickly into elohim city,

01:36:53.500 --> 01:36:57.480
and I was able to identify with

01:36:58.517 --> 01:37:03.090
their concept of life,
because I was looking

01:37:03.090 --> 01:37:05.923
for some answers to my own life.

01:37:06.960 --> 01:37:10.140
I saw Timothy McVeigh at elohim city

01:37:11.372 --> 01:37:15.857
eight weeks prior to the
Oklahoma city bombing.

01:37:15.857 --> 01:37:17.460
And I remember him distinctly,

01:37:17.460 --> 01:37:20.740
because he has a distinct face.

01:37:20.740 --> 01:37:22.670
But he was smilin', he was smilin',

01:37:22.670 --> 01:37:24.810
he was happy as he could be.

01:37:24.810 --> 01:37:27.530
These people were loaded for bear,

01:37:27.530 --> 01:37:30.053
and they were ready,
and they meant business.

01:37:30.970 --> 01:37:34.850
I believe the mindset at elohim city was,

01:37:34.850 --> 01:37:36.650
they didn't give a damn whether they were

01:37:36.650 --> 01:37:38.267
implicated in it or not.

01:37:39.460 --> 01:37:42.180
- What was interesting, and I think no one

01:37:42.180 --> 01:37:45.820
has paid any attention to it,
is that the CIA was involved

01:37:45.820 --> 01:37:47.490
at elohim city.

01:37:47.490 --> 01:37:48.560
Not only were they involved,

01:37:48.560 --> 01:37:52.070
but they had the spy satellites,

01:37:52.070 --> 01:37:54.057
the national geospatial
intelligence agency.

01:37:54.057 --> 01:37:57.150
I'd never heard of 'em before,
they run the spy satellites.

01:37:57.150 --> 01:38:00.180
They had them over elohim city.

01:38:00.180 --> 01:38:03.510
I think one of the things
that may be most productive

01:38:03.510 --> 01:38:05.863
to getting at the truth was the discovery

01:38:05.863 --> 01:38:08.560
of an operation the FBI had in place

01:38:08.560 --> 01:38:13.500
since about 1991 called
patcon, p-a-t-c-o-n.

01:38:13.500 --> 01:38:15.503
It's short for patriot conspiracy.

01:38:16.520 --> 01:38:21.310
It was an idea they had to
infiltrate every militia group,

01:38:21.310 --> 01:38:24.570
every Neo-Nazi group, every group critical

01:38:24.570 --> 01:38:27.200
of the government in the United States.

01:38:27.200 --> 01:38:29.780
The plan, apparently,
was to put informants

01:38:29.780 --> 01:38:32.660
in with all of these groups.

01:38:32.660 --> 01:38:37.660
And I think elohim city
was a patcon operation.

01:38:40.190 --> 01:38:43.060
I think McVeigh was
obviously involved in it.

01:38:43.060 --> 01:38:46.530
Now, whether he was a target
or an operative, I don't know,

01:38:46.530 --> 01:38:48.563
any more than I know whether
the government intended

01:38:48.563 --> 01:38:50.223
to blow up the murrah building.

01:38:51.060 --> 01:38:53.180
But they knew it was gonna happen,

01:38:53.180 --> 01:38:55.710
and they knew McVeigh was gonna do it.

01:38:55.710 --> 01:38:57.690
And they don't stop him.

01:38:57.690 --> 01:38:59.567
As alleged
in David Hoffman's book,

01:38:59.567 --> 01:39:02.420
"the Oklahoma city bombing
and the politics of terror,"

01:39:02.420 --> 01:39:04.790
strassmeir first aroused
suspicion that he was

01:39:04.790 --> 01:39:07.530
an undercover operative
when he was caught in Texas

01:39:07.530 --> 01:39:10.720
entering a federal building
at night with a key code.

01:39:10.720 --> 01:39:13.113
Did he have access to
the murrah building also?

01:39:14.041 --> 01:39:17.440
- When we interviewed Jane
Graham, who was a survivor,

01:39:17.440 --> 01:39:19.470
she said that when she went to work,

01:39:19.470 --> 01:39:21.690
it was either the day
before or two days before,

01:39:21.690 --> 01:39:22.980
I don't remember which,

01:39:22.980 --> 01:39:24.670
she parked in the basement parking,

01:39:24.670 --> 01:39:26.750
and when she got out of her
car, and was walking across

01:39:26.750 --> 01:39:30.240
the parking garage, she
saw three guys down there

01:39:30.240 --> 01:39:35.240
wearing coveralls and
placing putty on the columns,

01:39:35.380 --> 01:39:37.480
and stringing wire between the putty.

01:39:37.480 --> 01:39:39.670
Later, she picks out one of the guys

01:39:39.670 --> 01:39:41.930
from photographs and says, "that's him,"

01:39:41.930 --> 01:39:43.670
and it was Andreas strassmeir.

01:39:43.670 --> 01:39:47.350
- Strassmeir was there
listening, going over the plans.

01:39:47.350 --> 01:39:50.240
He was listening to everything, he was,

01:39:50.240 --> 01:39:52.280
what they were talking
about, looking at place,

01:39:52.280 --> 01:39:55.070
pointing to things, but
when they were talking,

01:39:55.070 --> 01:39:57.599
whatever they happened to
finally be talking about,

01:39:57.599 --> 01:40:01.010
and when I was looking at him,
at that point, then he left

01:40:01.010 --> 01:40:02.520
and went over to the other
side of the building,

01:40:02.520 --> 01:40:04.490
so I wouldn't keep watching him.

01:40:04.490 --> 01:40:07.460
The second man that was there,
who appeared to be military,

01:40:07.460 --> 01:40:11.440
he's the one that the man in
charge told to put the stuff

01:40:11.440 --> 01:40:13.020
back in the car.

01:40:13.020 --> 01:40:16.220
The second man, obviously,
was taking orders

01:40:16.220 --> 01:40:18.890
form the first man, because
he had wire in his hands,

01:40:18.890 --> 01:40:20.650
which I thought was telephone wire.

01:40:20.650 --> 01:40:25.290
It's that real light color,
thin wire, and he also had

01:40:25.290 --> 01:40:26.940
what appeared to be gray putty.

01:40:26.940 --> 01:40:30.270
- Well, that's exactly how
you string composition c4

01:40:30.270 --> 01:40:31.203
with det cord.

01:40:32.630 --> 01:40:34.630
- And the details are chilling.

01:40:34.630 --> 01:40:36.440
We'll also focus on surveillance cameras,

01:40:36.440 --> 01:40:38.890
cameras that caught the bombing on tape,

01:40:38.890 --> 01:40:41.000
and maybe the men behind the bombing.

01:40:41.000 --> 01:40:42.650
News channel has new information tonight

01:40:42.650 --> 01:40:44.580
that there is a chance
surveillance tapes could be

01:40:44.580 --> 01:40:47.469
the smoking-gun evidence,
and we ask candid questions

01:40:47.469 --> 01:40:50.550
in a rare face-to-face
meeting with atf officials

01:40:50.550 --> 01:40:51.792
close to the investigation.

01:40:51.792 --> 01:40:54.990
We learned that video collected
from downtown businesses

01:40:54.990 --> 01:40:57.015
the morning of April 19th may someday

01:40:57.015 --> 01:40:59.150
be played before a jury.

01:40:59.150 --> 01:41:01.330
Officials won't say who or
what, exactly, is on the tape.

01:41:01.330 --> 01:41:04.653
However, numerous sources have
confirmed the tapes exist,

01:41:04.653 --> 01:41:08.070
and that they reveal more than one bomber.

01:41:08.070 --> 01:41:10.880
- And I said, "I want two
other things from the FBI.

01:41:10.880 --> 01:41:14.173
I want the tapes from
the surveillance cameras,

01:41:15.504 --> 01:41:18.810
leading to the murrah building
on the day of the bombing,

01:41:18.810 --> 01:41:21.150
on the different buildings
around the murrah building,

01:41:21.150 --> 01:41:23.436
and I want the tapes from the cameras

01:41:23.436 --> 01:41:25.010
on the murrah building."

01:41:25.010 --> 01:41:28.570
Because I had received a
government document that said

01:41:28.570 --> 01:41:32.280
surveillance cameras
show the bomb detonating

01:41:32.280 --> 01:41:35.410
three minutes and six
seconds after the suspects

01:41:35.410 --> 01:41:37.100
exited the truck.

01:41:37.100 --> 01:41:39.653
Suspects, not one, plural.

01:41:41.100 --> 01:41:42.863
The fight now is over those tapes.

01:41:44.000 --> 01:41:46.007
They don't deny they exist, they just say,

01:41:46.007 --> 01:41:47.330
"we can't find 'em."

01:41:48.440 --> 01:41:53.060
Now, the notion that
this is the biggest crime

01:41:53.060 --> 01:41:54.710
the bureau had ever investigated,

01:41:56.199 --> 01:41:57.299
to that point in time,

01:41:59.138 --> 01:42:01.493
the largest mass murder
in American history.

01:42:02.560 --> 01:42:05.330
The two most important
pieces of evidence you have,

01:42:05.330 --> 01:42:07.670
the arrest of McVeigh, and the videotape

01:42:07.670 --> 01:42:10.860
showing McVeigh delivering the
bomb to the murrah building,

01:42:10.860 --> 01:42:13.493
you can't find?

01:42:15.040 --> 01:42:16.630
Incredible.

01:42:16.630 --> 01:42:20.760
- The enhanced photo shows
a very distinct possibility

01:42:20.760 --> 01:42:23.090
of a man standing behind that truck,

01:42:23.090 --> 01:42:26.620
and the time-sequence camera
took additional photographs.

01:42:26.620 --> 01:42:28.780
So will those additional photographs show

01:42:28.780 --> 01:42:30.040
there was a man there?

01:42:30.040 --> 01:42:31.690
Will they show that he was alone?

01:42:31.690 --> 01:42:33.930
Will it show it was the
suspect, Tim McVeigh?

01:42:33.930 --> 01:42:35.390
The additional photographs in the trial

01:42:35.390 --> 01:42:36.710
should help point that out.

01:42:36.710 --> 01:42:38.690
- I think one of the things
that stands out to me

01:42:38.690 --> 01:42:42.350
is the fact that, during
that first morning,

01:42:42.350 --> 01:42:44.930
while we were being held at bay

01:42:44.930 --> 01:42:46.482
from doing any recovery work,

01:42:46.482 --> 01:42:50.563
there were FBI agents, or at
least, men in FBI raid jackets,

01:42:52.030 --> 01:42:55.250
dismantling the video cameras
off the side of the building.

01:42:55.250 --> 01:42:59.040
- I'm Charlie Rose, i'm
with legend video transfer,

01:42:59.040 --> 01:43:03.150
and the FBI had employed me

01:43:03.150 --> 01:43:05.780
to duplicate a number of videos

01:43:05.780 --> 01:43:09.950
for them, shortly after
the murrah bombing.

01:43:09.950 --> 01:43:14.450
I was asked to duplicate
approximately 400 tapes

01:43:14.450 --> 01:43:16.110
for the FBI.

01:43:16.110 --> 01:43:21.040
We had two FBI agents in the office.

01:43:21.040 --> 01:43:24.680
We had two studios set up for duplication,

01:43:24.680 --> 01:43:29.680
and each FBI agent was
required to stay in the room

01:43:30.300 --> 01:43:33.730
with each of us that were in that room.

01:43:33.730 --> 01:43:35.070
Really didn't have the opportunity

01:43:35.070 --> 01:43:37.420
to sit back and watch the videos.

01:43:37.420 --> 01:43:40.880
There's probably a lot to
learn, you know, from the videos

01:43:40.880 --> 01:43:42.210
that they saw.

01:43:42.210 --> 01:43:46.090
Some of 'em are meaningless,
but others, you know,

01:43:46.090 --> 01:43:50.680
could make some powerful impact

01:43:50.680 --> 01:43:55.610
on what actually happened.

01:43:55.610 --> 01:43:58.240
- The government will not release the film

01:43:58.240 --> 01:44:01.310
that was in the video cameras
on the front of the building

01:44:01.310 --> 01:44:05.470
that would show whether I
was accurate or not accurate.

01:44:05.470 --> 01:44:06.320
- Of course, the other achilles heel

01:44:06.320 --> 01:44:08.860
is the videotapes of the building itself,

01:44:08.860 --> 01:44:10.220
from the different surveillance cameras,

01:44:10.220 --> 01:44:11.910
that no one's seen.

01:44:11.910 --> 01:44:16.500
If McVeigh was Lee Harvey
McVeigh, all by himself,

01:44:16.500 --> 01:44:19.802
the lone nut with a truck,
then why don't they show us

01:44:19.802 --> 01:44:21.090
the videotapes of the truck?

01:44:21.090 --> 01:44:22.590
Show us the videotapes of him gettin' out,

01:44:22.590 --> 01:44:24.550
or was there more than him in the truck?

01:44:24.550 --> 01:44:28.580
- There were, like, 20,
22 films in the area

01:44:28.580 --> 01:44:31.310
that were confiscated by the FBI

01:44:33.180 --> 01:44:36.450
that would have shown the
truck bein' pulled up,

01:44:36.450 --> 01:44:37.810
people gettin' out of the truck.

01:44:37.810 --> 01:44:40.650
It would have shown what
was goin' on at the time

01:44:40.650 --> 01:44:43.130
the explosions took place, and obviously,

01:44:43.130 --> 01:44:48.025
they confiscated those,
and it doesn't take much

01:44:48.025 --> 01:44:51.600
to figure out that the federal authorities

01:44:51.600 --> 01:44:53.040
weren't trying to get to the truth,

01:44:53.040 --> 01:44:55.110
they seemed to be covering up things.

01:44:55.110 --> 01:44:59.500
- Their first objective
is to protect the agency.

01:44:59.500 --> 01:45:02.640
Not to do what's right, not to do justice,

01:45:02.640 --> 01:45:03.743
not to serve the American people.

01:45:03.743 --> 01:45:05.323
It's to protect themselves.

01:45:06.170 --> 01:45:08.913
And they will do anything,
anything, to do that.

01:45:17.350 --> 01:45:18.920
Tim McVeigh
was honorably discharged

01:45:18.920 --> 01:45:21.110
from the army three
years before the bombing,

01:45:21.110 --> 01:45:23.880
leaving behind an
exemplary service record.

01:45:23.880 --> 01:45:25.970
After a brief but
intense combat experience

01:45:25.970 --> 01:45:27.470
in the persian Gulf war,

01:45:27.470 --> 01:45:29.920
McVeigh tried out for the special forces.

01:45:29.920 --> 01:45:32.420
He pronounced himself unable to continue

01:45:32.420 --> 01:45:34.410
just a few days into the testing,

01:45:34.410 --> 01:45:37.180
and returned to his unit
demoralized and, some say,

01:45:37.180 --> 01:45:38.980
a changed man.

01:45:38.980 --> 01:45:42.340
- Through being able to see
Timothy McVeigh's letters

01:45:42.340 --> 01:45:43.460
to his defense team,

01:45:43.460 --> 01:45:45.910
this is really behind-the-scenes stuff,

01:45:45.910 --> 01:45:48.250
letters to his family,

01:45:48.250 --> 01:45:52.270
the memos the defense team
writes, which detail his mood

01:45:52.270 --> 01:45:53.430
from day to day.

01:45:53.430 --> 01:45:55.430
Some of the medical reports,
while he's in prison,

01:45:55.430 --> 01:45:57.390
which detail his thoughts.

01:45:57.390 --> 01:45:59.040
On the one hand, you have the McVeigh

01:45:59.040 --> 01:46:00.910
who's mad at the government,
on the other hand,

01:46:00.910 --> 01:46:03.270
you have the McVeigh who
works for the government.

01:46:03.270 --> 01:46:06.410
The defense team themselves
could never obtain

01:46:06.410 --> 01:46:09.610
his full military records,
and that even though

01:46:09.610 --> 01:46:11.890
they were ordered by a judge.

01:46:11.890 --> 01:46:12.850
- Where does he turn up?

01:46:12.850 --> 01:46:15.330
He turns up in buffalo, New York,

01:46:15.330 --> 01:46:17.740
and while's he's up there,
he creates what's known

01:46:17.740 --> 01:46:19.000
as a legend.

01:46:19.000 --> 01:46:21.830
Now, a legend is when you go undercover,

01:46:21.830 --> 01:46:22.840
or you get sheep-dipped.

01:46:22.840 --> 01:46:24.920
Sheep-dipped means you
change your identity,

01:46:24.920 --> 01:46:27.310
you change your, who you work for,

01:46:27.310 --> 01:46:28.820
and become a new person.

01:46:28.820 --> 01:46:31.440
Changes his personality up
there, and all of a sudden,

01:46:31.440 --> 01:46:35.130
he's ranting and raving
about the Turner diaries,

01:46:35.130 --> 01:46:36.400
and overthrowing the government,

01:46:36.400 --> 01:46:38.167
and all this other nonsense,
to where they're goin'

01:46:38.167 --> 01:46:39.490
"this guy's a wacko."

01:46:39.490 --> 01:46:42.340
He works up there six
months and disappears.

01:46:42.340 --> 01:46:44.270
Where do we find him again?

01:46:44.270 --> 01:46:46.320
Going into militia meetings
and doing the same thing.

01:46:46.320 --> 01:46:47.630
Making sure he's noticed.

01:46:47.630 --> 01:46:50.350
- If you look at Lee Harvey
oswald and Tim McVeigh,

01:46:50.350 --> 01:46:52.410
and other patsies, they're very similar.

01:46:52.410 --> 01:46:56.163
They're in the military, they
have security clearances.

01:46:57.070 --> 01:46:58.600
McVeigh wrote
a letter to his sister,

01:46:58.600 --> 01:47:01.010
who turned it over to the
FBI, in which he admits

01:47:01.010 --> 01:47:03.530
that he was selected out
of special forces training

01:47:03.530 --> 01:47:05.800
to participate in covert operations,

01:47:05.800 --> 01:47:08.160
to help run drugs to
fund these operations,

01:47:08.160 --> 01:47:11.060
and to assassinate security risks.

01:47:11.060 --> 01:47:14.380
Mere bravado, or was
McVeigh telling the truth?

01:47:14.380 --> 01:47:19.380
- The FBI had put wiretaps
on the McVeigh family's phone

01:47:19.840 --> 01:47:20.890
after the bombing,

01:47:20.890 --> 01:47:24.150
and so, I'm reading this
conversation back and forth

01:47:24.150 --> 01:47:25.820
between his mother and his sister.

01:47:25.820 --> 01:47:27.730
There's actually a few
of these conversations

01:47:27.730 --> 01:47:31.460
where they say, "we don't understand

01:47:31.460 --> 01:47:34.340
why the FBI won't listen to us,

01:47:34.340 --> 01:47:36.180
and why the media is reporting

01:47:36.180 --> 01:47:38.980
that Timothy McVeigh
washed out, or dropped out,

01:47:38.980 --> 01:47:40.390
of special forces."

01:47:40.390 --> 01:47:43.080
They're saying, "no, we were told

01:47:43.080 --> 01:47:45.860
that he was still active in the military,

01:47:45.860 --> 01:47:49.280
and that he was working
on these covert missions."

01:47:49.280 --> 01:47:51.130
- And he told his family,
he told many others,

01:47:51.130 --> 01:47:53.384
Terry Nichols, who signed an affidavit,

01:47:53.384 --> 01:47:56.320
that McVeigh believed he was
out there infiltrating militias

01:47:56.320 --> 01:47:59.618
and right-wing groups, and
was preparing to set 'em up.

01:47:59.618 --> 01:48:01.130
And then, of course, he later learned

01:48:01.130 --> 01:48:03.740
that he was the guy that got set up.

01:48:03.740 --> 01:48:05.850
If McVeigh was
working for the government,

01:48:05.850 --> 01:48:07.290
what are we to make of the involvement

01:48:07.290 --> 01:48:10.093
of Terry Nichols, the
only convicted accomplice?

01:48:11.010 --> 01:48:12.710
- When Nichols had been convicted,

01:48:13.550 --> 01:48:15.590
but not given the death penalty,

01:48:15.590 --> 01:48:17.683
in federal court and in state court,

01:48:18.810 --> 01:48:20.210
he could not be tried again.

01:48:22.480 --> 01:48:25.580
He wrote to Attorney General,

01:48:25.580 --> 01:48:27.577
then-Attorney General
John ashcroft and said,

01:48:27.577 --> 01:48:29.957
"come and see me, come and see me,

01:48:29.957 --> 01:48:31.557
and I'll tell you all about it."

01:48:32.400 --> 01:48:34.727
In his
declaration, Nichols stated that

01:48:34.727 --> 01:48:37.120
"crucial parts of this
terrorist attack remain hidden

01:48:37.120 --> 01:48:39.770
from the American people,
especially the identities

01:48:39.770 --> 01:48:42.110
of 'others unknown,' who
collaborated with McVeigh

01:48:42.110 --> 01:48:43.490
in the bombing."

01:48:43.490 --> 01:48:45.470
McVeigh told Nichols that
he had been recruited

01:48:45.470 --> 01:48:48.400
to perform undercover missions
while in the U.S. army.

01:48:48.400 --> 01:48:51.340
Always the good soldier,
McVeigh revealed only one name

01:48:51.340 --> 01:48:53.630
in his chain of command: Larry potts,

01:48:53.630 --> 01:48:56.480
assistant director of the
FBI, and the lead agent

01:48:56.480 --> 01:48:59.330
on the Ruby Ridge catastrophe in 1992,

01:48:59.330 --> 01:49:02.530
in which a U.S. marshal
and 14-year-old Sam Weaver

01:49:02.530 --> 01:49:04.630
and his mother, Vicky Weaver, were killed.

01:49:05.560 --> 01:49:07.380
Larry potts later played an active role

01:49:07.380 --> 01:49:09.220
in the siege at waco.

01:49:09.220 --> 01:49:12.020
McVeigh was angry at
potts for going off-script

01:49:12.020 --> 01:49:14.020
and changing targets at the last minute.

01:49:15.910 --> 01:49:19.540
Another telling clue is on Tim
McVeigh's death certificate.

01:49:19.540 --> 01:49:22.750
Despite being officially out
of the military for nine years,

01:49:22.750 --> 01:49:25.050
and having held many
different jobs since then,

01:49:25.050 --> 01:49:27.767
his listed occupation was "U.S. army."

01:49:29.400 --> 01:49:32.710
So why did Tim McVeigh take
the fall for his accomplices?

01:49:32.710 --> 01:49:35.170
Perhaps the intervention
of a known psychological

01:49:35.170 --> 01:49:38.003
warfare expert explains
his silence till the end.

01:49:38.950 --> 01:49:43.150
- The record clearly
shows that Dr. Jolyon west

01:49:43.150 --> 01:49:46.660
consulted Timothy McVeigh's defense team.

01:49:46.660 --> 01:49:51.090
Dr. West had previously been
psychiatrist and consultant

01:49:51.090 --> 01:49:55.690
for Patty hearst, sirhan
sirhan, and Jack Ruby.

01:49:55.690 --> 01:49:58.260
- We know that jolyon
west was considered to be

01:49:58.260 --> 01:50:01.604
the number-two mind control
expert in North America,

01:50:01.604 --> 01:50:04.720
under only Dr. Ewen Cameron.

01:50:04.720 --> 01:50:07.950
- Dr. West came under a lot of scrutiny

01:50:07.950 --> 01:50:11.390
during his time as chief
of psychiatry at ucla

01:50:11.390 --> 01:50:15.340
because he was proposing using prisoners,

01:50:15.340 --> 01:50:18.860
the general community,
poor people, minorities,

01:50:18.860 --> 01:50:20.810
as test subjects.

01:50:20.810 --> 01:50:22.880
And then, west's career
continues to flourish

01:50:22.880 --> 01:50:24.820
through the '80s, and he
continues his research

01:50:24.820 --> 01:50:28.219
into hypnosis, branches out
into terrorism and cults,

01:50:28.219 --> 01:50:30.100
even consulting, and later writing

01:50:30.100 --> 01:50:31.730
about the waco massacre.

01:50:31.730 --> 01:50:34.870
- Dr. John Smith, if
that's even his real name,

01:50:34.870 --> 01:50:37.690
was the protégé of Dr. Jolyon west,

01:50:37.690 --> 01:50:39.320
Mr. Mind control,

01:50:39.320 --> 01:50:43.280
and he was McVeigh's doctor in prison.

01:50:43.280 --> 01:50:45.010
Today, it's reported that he

01:50:45.010 --> 01:50:46.730
is one of the head psychiatrists,

01:50:46.730 --> 01:50:49.350
one of the head doctors,
at Guantanamo bay.

01:50:49.350 --> 01:50:51.957
The fact that you've got the protégé

01:50:51.957 --> 01:50:54.740
of one of the fathers
of modern mind control

01:50:54.740 --> 01:50:56.970
now being the head of
psychiatry at Guantanamo bay,

01:50:56.970 --> 01:50:59.540
which is an admitted
mind-control laboratory,

01:50:59.540 --> 01:51:00.760
that's even mainstream news,

01:51:00.760 --> 01:51:04.000
I mean, you couldn't make
this up in a spy novel.

01:51:04.000 --> 01:51:05.900
Truth is always stranger than fiction,

01:51:05.900 --> 01:51:07.600
and it's all hidden in plain view.

01:51:13.980 --> 01:51:15.190
Was the bombing the product

01:51:15.190 --> 01:51:16.630
of a sting gone out of control,

01:51:16.630 --> 01:51:18.550
with McVeigh taking the blame for a series

01:51:18.550 --> 01:51:19.700
of government failures?

01:51:20.760 --> 01:51:23.330
- They kind of set up a sting operation,

01:51:23.330 --> 01:51:26.830
it appears to me, that went bad.

01:51:26.830 --> 01:51:31.070
They thought they would
stop you know, the efforts

01:51:31.070 --> 01:51:34.730
of strassmeir, millar, and
others through elohim city.

01:51:34.730 --> 01:51:36.650
- I eventually talked
to this senate staffer,

01:51:36.650 --> 01:51:40.240
and he informed me that
the Oklahoma city bombing

01:51:40.240 --> 01:51:43.130
was actually a sting
operation that went wrong,

01:51:43.130 --> 01:51:45.290
and that the effort to cover it up

01:51:45.290 --> 01:51:48.690
was because they were not able
to stop the sting operation.

01:51:48.690 --> 01:51:51.910
- When it fell apart, in
that they weren't able

01:51:51.910 --> 01:51:54.870
to stop it right before it took place

01:51:54.870 --> 01:51:57.990
and proclaim to the public
how great they were,

01:51:57.990 --> 01:51:59.950
so they could get new funding for the atf,

01:51:59.950 --> 01:52:03.320
because the atf had lost
so much credibility,

01:52:03.320 --> 01:52:06.023
due to the Randy Weaver situation.

01:52:07.560 --> 01:52:09.510
- I don't know if anybody'll ever know.

01:52:10.410 --> 01:52:11.710
I know my brother was killed.

01:52:11.710 --> 01:52:13.670
I'm often asked why, why, why?

01:52:13.670 --> 01:52:16.100
I know my brother was killed
for information he didn't have

01:52:16.100 --> 01:52:17.053
about the bombing.

01:52:18.890 --> 01:52:21.390
Why the people in the
murrah building were killed,

01:52:22.850 --> 01:52:24.710
as I said, I don't know
if they intended it,

01:52:24.710 --> 01:52:26.447
or it just got away from 'em.

01:52:29.453 --> 01:52:31.903
God, I hate to think that
they did it on purpose.

01:52:33.150 --> 01:52:34.690
Perhaps it
was a deliberate attack

01:52:34.690 --> 01:52:37.120
by a criminal element in this government,

01:52:37.120 --> 01:52:39.380
using the reins of power
to execute and cover up

01:52:39.380 --> 01:52:40.960
their crime.

01:52:40.960 --> 01:52:45.340
- In 2006, the American
behavioral scientist published

01:52:45.340 --> 01:52:48.910
the whole journal on this concept

01:52:48.910 --> 01:52:49.810
that's being developed

01:52:49.810 --> 01:52:52.240
called a state crime against democracy,

01:52:52.240 --> 01:52:53.510
scad, for short.

01:52:53.510 --> 01:52:56.770
There's a recognition,
a growing recognition,

01:52:56.770 --> 01:53:01.770
among academia that, oftentimes,
people have not pursued

01:53:03.910 --> 01:53:08.090
culpability into elite crimes
for the fear of being called

01:53:08.090 --> 01:53:09.850
a conspiracy theorist.

01:53:09.850 --> 01:53:13.330
When there is a state
crime against the people,

01:53:13.330 --> 01:53:15.640
what generally happens is that inquiries

01:53:15.640 --> 01:53:18.680
into these crimes tend
to be highly controlled,

01:53:18.680 --> 01:53:22.350
tightly framed, and be totally reliant

01:53:22.350 --> 01:53:26.720
on agencies who stand to be
embarrassed by investigations.

01:53:26.720 --> 01:53:27.850
- It's now been declassified

01:53:27.850 --> 01:53:30.180
that the Gulf of tonkin in 1964,

01:53:30.180 --> 01:53:31.950
to get the United States fully committed

01:53:31.950 --> 01:53:34.600
into the Vietnam war, was a staged event,

01:53:34.600 --> 01:53:36.410
and those lbj tapes have been released,

01:53:36.410 --> 01:53:39.266
where, days before McNamara
is telling him on the phone

01:53:39.266 --> 01:53:41.090
how they're going to stage the event

01:53:41.090 --> 01:53:42.540
to get the United States into the war,

01:53:42.540 --> 01:53:45.730
and what he would need to say
at those press conferences.

01:53:45.730 --> 01:53:49.440
In early 1995, the entire United States

01:53:49.440 --> 01:53:52.060
was politically awakening.

01:53:52.060 --> 01:53:55.230
The population was angry about waco.

01:53:55.230 --> 01:53:58.060
They were angry about the United States

01:53:58.060 --> 01:54:01.310
losing its sovereignty, and
Bill Clinton trying to pass

01:54:01.310 --> 01:54:04.190
anti-second amendment legislation.

01:54:04.190 --> 01:54:06.870
The federal government was
forced to basically come in

01:54:06.870 --> 01:54:10.069
and create a crisis so
they could demonize anyone

01:54:10.069 --> 01:54:12.919
who thought the government
was too big or out of control.

01:54:14.040 --> 01:54:18.630
In 1994 and 1995, the congress
had tried, unsuccessfully,

01:54:18.630 --> 01:54:20.280
to pass their omnibus crime bill,

01:54:20.280 --> 01:54:23.220
that expanded federal jurisdiction,

01:54:23.220 --> 01:54:25.160
that went after the second amendment,

01:54:25.160 --> 01:54:27.780
that was going to create all these new

01:54:27.780 --> 01:54:30.900
federal agencies to spy
on the American people.

01:54:30.900 --> 01:54:31.930
And that was one of the reasons

01:54:31.930 --> 01:54:32.840
that Oklahoma and other states

01:54:32.840 --> 01:54:33.830
were upset, they understood

01:54:33.830 --> 01:54:35.720
this was totally unconstitutional,

01:54:35.720 --> 01:54:38.730
and a huge federal overreach,

01:54:38.730 --> 01:54:40.510
and it violated the 10th amendment.

01:54:40.510 --> 01:54:44.081
But after the Oklahoma
city bombing tragedy,

01:54:44.081 --> 01:54:46.321
suddenly, they were able to rename it

01:54:46.321 --> 01:54:50.150
as the antiterrorism and
effective death penalty act,

01:54:50.150 --> 01:54:52.580
and that was able to sell through.

01:54:52.580 --> 01:54:54.170
- Well, I think one of
the things we'll be seeing

01:54:54.170 --> 01:54:55.470
over the next few weeks and months

01:54:55.470 --> 01:54:58.450
are new legislation, both to deal with

01:54:58.450 --> 01:55:01.030
domestic groups and
international terrorism.

01:55:01.030 --> 01:55:04.563
